{"type":"message","id":"75b19b5d","parentId":"6473d549","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:15:09.930Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-02-03 17:15 UTC] BLUEPRINT A/B TEST — GAMMA (Hybrid Approach)\n\nYou are running Test Gamma for the Bellevue Standpipe project. Your approach: HYBRID - Start from bid structure, but validate with full document extraction.\n\nPROJECT: NYC H+H Fire Pump and Standpipe Replacement - Bellevue Hospital\nPROJECT PATH: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/\n\nPREVIOUS TEST RESULTS (use these as reference):\n- test-alpha-results.json (Bid-First): Found 7 standpipes, 5 RFIs\n- test-beta-results.json (Doc-First): Found 6 standpipes, 8 RFIs\n- DISCREPANCY: Standpipe count differs! Your job is to resolve this.\n\nHYBRID METHODOLOGY:\n\nPHASE 1: Load Bid Structure\n- Read bid-breakdown-mapped.json (95 items, 10 fire protection items)\n- This is your deliverable framework — every finding must map to a bid item\n\nPHASE 2: Full Document Extraction (parallel validation)\n- Read the extracted specs from /extracted/ folder (Beta already extracted these)\n- Cross-reference against bid items\n- Flag any scope in docs NOT in bid breakdown\n- Flag any bid items NOT found in docs\n\nPHASE 3: Resolve Discrepancies\n- CRITICAL: Determine actual standpipe count (6 or 7?)\n- Check Alternates 1-6 in specs and drawings\n- Document the source of truth for each finding\n\nPHASE 4: Expert Analysis with Validation\n- Read /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/experts/fire-protection/EXPERT.md\n- For each bid item (43-51, 95), provide:\n  - Quantity/scope from BOTH bid structure AND document extraction\n  - Confidence level (High/Medium/Low)\n  - Source citation (spec section, drawing number)\n  - Any conflicts between sources\n\nPHASE 5: Unified Output\n- Merge findings into single authoritative takeoff\n- RFI list with priority ranking\n- Coordination items with responsible trade\n- Confidence score per line item\n\nOUTPUT: Write to /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/test-gamma-results.json\n\nKEY METRICS TO TRACK:\n- Time elapsed\n- Documents referenced\n- Bid items fully validated (with source citations)\n- Discrepancies resolved\n- Final confidence score\n\nThe goal: Prove that Hybrid gives HIGHER CONFIDENCE than either approach alone.\n\nReport back with comparison to Alpha and Beta results."}],"timestamp":1770138909929}}
