ed Standpipe and Sprinkler System\",\n      \"project_scope\": \"Complete replacement of fire pump and standpipe risers in 23-story hospital building\",\n      \"standpipes\": {\n        \"total\": 6,\n        \"base_bid\": 1,\n        \"alternates\": 5,\n        \"class\": \"Class I (per spec)\",\n        \"height\": \"~276 feet (Cellar to Penthouse)\"\n      },\n      \"fire_pump\": {\n        \"type\": \"Horizontal split-case centrifugal\",\n        \"driver\": \"Electric\",\n        \"controller\": \"Soft-start with automatic transfer switch\",\n        \"jockey_pump\": \"Yes, included\",\n        \"location\": \"Cellar fire pump room\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"key_specifications\": {\n      \"reference_standards\": [\n        \"NFPA 13 (2016) - Sprinkler Systems\",\n        \"NFPA 14 (2016) - Standpipes\",\n        \"NFPA 20 - Fire Pumps\",\n        \"NFPA 25 - ITM\",\n        \"NYC Building Code 2022\",\n        \"NYC Fire Code 2022\"\n      ],\n      \"pipe_materials\": \"ASTM A53/A795 black steel, Schedule 40 galvanized\",\n      \"valves\": {\n        \"hose_connections\": \"2-1/2\\\" angle type with 1-1/2\\\" reducer\",\n        \"supervisory_switches\": \"Required on all control valves\",\n        \"pressure_restricting\": \"Set at 100 PSI where static > 100 PSI\"\n      },\n      \"cabinets\": {\n        \"standard\": \"Croker 1410 Series, 2-hour fire rated\",\n        \"detention\": \"Potter Roemer DC1810-F, heavy-duty security type\",\n        \"lobby\": \"Storage cabinet with FDNY equipment\"\n      },\n      \"warranties\": {\n        \"standpipes_and_valves\": \"5 years\",\n        \"fire_pumps\": \"5 years\",\n        \"maintenance_service\": \"5 years from substantial completion\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"drawing_coverage\": {\n      \"removal_plans\": 28,\n      \"new_work_plans\": 28,\n      \"riser_diagrams\": 4,\n      \"details\": 4,\n      \"pump_room\": 1\n    }\n  },\n  \"flags_and_issues\": {\n    \"conflicts\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-001\",\n        \"severity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Fire pump delivery - spec states pump must be delivered 'broken down' due to cellar access limitations at stair turns. Rigging plan required before work.\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"21 30 00, 2.01.D\",\n        \"action\": \"Verify access route and submit rigging plan\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-002\",\n        \"severity\": \"high\",\n        \"description\": \"Asbestos abatement required in cellar and penthouse water tank room BEFORE fire protection work can proceed\",\n        \"drawing_ref\": \"AA-001 to AA-005\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"02 82 13\",\n        \"action\": \"Asbestos work must be coordinated and completed first\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-003\",\n        \"severity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Hospital operations cannot be disrupted during construction - requires careful phasing and maintaining fire protection\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"02 41 19, 1.11.A\",\n        \"action\": \"Detailed phasing plan coordination with facility manager\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"rfis_needed\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RFI-001\",\n        \"category\": \"Fire Pump\",\n        \"question\": \"Confirm fire pump capacity (GPM @ PSI) - spec says 'as listed on Design Drawings' but values not extracted from PDFs\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"21 30 00, 2.04.J\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RFI-002\",\n        \"category\": \"Standpipe\",\n        \"question\": \"Confirm all 6 standpipes are Class I - spec mentions Class I but also references Class I, II, III requirements\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"21 12 00, 2.05.A\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RFI-003\",\n        \"category\": \"PRV\",\n        \"question\": \"Confirm floors requiring pressure-restricting devices - pressure > 100 PSI at which floors?\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"21 12 00, 2.04.F\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RFI-004\",\n        \"category\": \"Alternates\",\n        \"question\": \"Clarify if Alternates 5 and 6 are additional standpipes or other building areas - partial text in drawings\",\n        \"drawing_ref\": \"FP-001\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RFI-005\",\n        \"category\": \"Seismic\",\n        \"question\": \"Seismic bracing details not fully extracted - verify seismic design category and bracing requirements\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"21 30 00, 1.04.B\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RFI-006\",\n        \"category\": \"Hydraulic Calcs\",\n        \"question\": \"Contractor responsible for hydraulic calculations - confirm water supply data (flow test) availability\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"21 05 00, 1.01.A\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RFI-007\",\n        \"category\": \"FDC\",\n        \"question\": \"Confirm Fire Department Connection (FDC) type and location - flush vs exposed type?\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"21 12 00, 2.06\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RFI-008\",\n        \"category\": \"Controller\",\n        \"question\": \"Fire pump controller clearances and workspace - confirm NEMA enclosure type (Types 2 and 12 specified)\",\n        \"spec_ref\": \"21 30 00, 2.05.D\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"cost_drivers\": [\n      \"Fire pump assembly (horizontal split-case) - major equipment cost\",\n      \"Soft-start controller with ATS - premium over standard controller\",\n      \"5-year maintenance contract required per spec\",\n      \"Detention-type locked cabinets for secure areas (higher cost than standard)\",\n      \"2-hour fire-rated hose cabinets (premium product)\",\n      \"Hospital premium for phased work and after-hours scheduling\",\n      \"Asbestos abatement coordination (separate work, but impacts schedule)\"\n    ],\n    \"coordination_items\": [\n      {\n        \"trade\": \"Electrical (Div 26)\",\n        \"item\": \"Fire pump power feed and ATS connection\",\n        \"bid_items\": [79, 90]\n      },\n      {\n        \"trade\": \"Fire Alarm (Div 28)\",\n        \"item\": \"Valve supervisory switches, flow switches integration\",\n        \"bid_items\": [92]\n      },\n      {\n        \"trade\": \"Architectural (Div 09)\",\n        \"item\": \"Hose cabinet recesses, ceiling penetrations, firestopping\",\n        \"bid_items\": [27, 28, 34, 37]\n      },\n      {\n        \"trade\": \"Demolition (Div 02)\",\n        \"item\": \"Removal of existing standpipe and fire pump equipment\",\n        \"bid_items\": [19, 20]\n      },\n      {\n        \"trade\": \"Plumbing (Div 22)\",\n        \"item\": \"Water supply connection, domestic water isolation\",\n        \"bid_items\": [57, 58]\n      },\n      {\n        \"trade\": \"HVAC (Div 23)\",\n        \"item\": \"Fire pump room ventilation\",\n        \"bid_items\": [60, 76]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"bid_item_mapping\": {\n    \"fire_protection_items\": [\n      {\"item_no\": 43, \"description\": \"21 05 00 General Fire Suppression Requirements\", \"coverage\": \"Complete\", \"notes\": \"Extracted full spec section\"},\n      {\"item_no\": 44, \"description\": \"21 05 03 Pipes and Tubes for Fire Suppression\", \"coverage\": \"Complete\", \"notes\": \"Black steel, Sch 40 galvanized per spec\"},\n      {\"item_no\": 45, \"description\": \"21 05 04 Valves for Fire Suppression\", \"coverage\": \"Complete\", \"notes\": \"OS&Y, butterfly, check, hose valves detailed\"},\n      {\"item_no\": 46, \"description\": \"21 05 05 Hangers, Supports and Anchors\", \"coverage\": \"Complete\", \"notes\": \"Seismic requirements noted\"},\n      {\"item_no\": 47, \"description\": \"21 05 13 Common Motor Requirements\", \"coverage\": \"Complete\", \"notes\": \"Fire pump motor in spec\"},\n      {\"item_no\": 48, \"description\": \"21 05 48 Noise and Vibration Controls\", \"coverage\": \"Complete\", \"notes\": \"Isolators for fire pump\"},\n      {\"item_no\": 49, \"description\": \"21 12 00 Fire Suppression Standpipes\", \"coverage\": \"Complete\", \"notes\": \"Full spec extracted - 6 standpipes (1 base + 5 alt)\"},\n      {\"item_no\": 50, \"description\": \"21 13 13 Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems\", \"coverage\": \"Partial\", \"notes\": \"Referenced but limited sprinkler scope in this project\"},\n      {\"item_no\": 51, \"description\": \"21 30 00 Fire Pumps\", \"coverage\": \"Complete\", \"notes\": \"Full spec extracted - horiz split-case with controller\"},\n      {\"item_no\": 95, \"description\": \"Other Fire Protection\", \"coverage\": \"TBD\", \"notes\": \"May include testing, commissioning extras\"}\n    ],\n    \"scope_gaps\": [\n      {\n        \"item\": \"Fire pump testing and commissioning\",\n        \"notes\": \"Detailed in spec but no separate bid item - likely in Item 51\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"item\": \"Roof manifold\",\n        \"notes\": \"Spec 21 12 00 mentions roof manifold with 4 outlets - verify in bid\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"item\": \"Lobby storage cabinet equipment\",\n        \"notes\": \"FDNY required equipment (hose, nozzle, wrenches) - verify in bid\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"item\": \"Extra materials (2 hose nozzles/hoses)\",\n        \"notes\": \"Spec requires spare parts delivery - verify in bid\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"items_not_found_in_docs\": []\n  },\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"project_type\": \"Fire pump and standpipe replacement in active hospital\",\n    \"complexity\": \"High - 23 stories, occupied building, asbestos present\",\n    \"base_bid_scope\": \"Fire pump room + 1 standpipe riser\",\n    \"alternate_scope\": \"5 additional standpipe risers (Alternates 1-5), possible Alt 6 area\",\n    \"critical_path_items\": [\n      \"Asbestos abatement completion\",\n      \"Fire pump delivery and rigging\",\n      \"Maintaining fire protection during phased construction\"\n    ],\n    \"key_findings\": [\n      \"Comprehensive specification set with 2,388 pages\",\n      \"63 fire protection drawing sheets with removal and new work plans\",\n      \"6 bid alternates for standpipe work allowing flexible award\",\n      \"5-year warranty and maintenance contract required\",\n      \"NYC Fire Code compliance with FDNY thread requirements\",\n      \"Hospital occupancy requires careful phasing and protection\"\n    ],\n    \"recommendation\": \"Document-first approach successfully indexed all content; recommend visual drawing review for pipe sizes, exact quantities, and FDC locations\"\n  }\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138916703}}
{"type":"message","id":"6d367ac9","parentId":"75fcedc3","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:15:16.712Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01JWfHkaDyrupYpkeTjKSauU","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 🔥 Fire Protection Expert\n\n## Identity\n\nYou are the **Fire Protection Expert** for BluePrint, a construction takeoff AI system. You have deep expertise in fire suppression systems, standpipes, sprinklers, and life safety systems. You think like a veteran fire protection contractor who has estimated hundreds of projects.\n\n## Your Divisions\n\n| Division | Section | Coverage |\n|----------|---------|----------|\n| **21 00 00** | Fire Suppression | General requirements |\n| **21 10 00** | Water-Based Systems | Sprinklers, standpipes |\n| **21 11 00** | Facility Fire Pumps | Fire pump assemblies |\n| **21 12 00** | Fire-Suppression Standpipes | Standpipe systems |\n| **21 13 00** | Fire-Suppression Sprinkler Systems | Wet, dry, preaction, deluge |\n| **21 20 00** | Fire-Extinguishing Systems | Clean agent, CO2, foam |\n| **21 30 00** | Fire Pumps | Pump specifications |\n\n## Your Drawings\n\n**Primary Focus:**\n- FP-series (Fire Protection plans)\n- FP-001 through FP-999\n\n**Cross-Reference (coordination):**\n- A-series: Floor plans for coverage areas, ceiling heights\n- M-series: Mechanical rooms, duct locations (clearances)\n- P-series: Domestic water tie-ins, combined services\n- S-series: Structural penetrations, hanger points\n- E-series: Fire alarm integration points\n\n## Your Specifications\n\n**Primary Sections:**\n- 21 00 00 – Fire Suppression (general)\n- 21 05 00 – Common Work Results\n- 21 05 13 – Motors for Fire Suppression\n- 21 05 29 – Hangers/Supports for Fire Suppression\n- 21 05 48 – Vibration/Seismic Control\n- 21 10 00 – Water-Based Systems\n- 21 11 00 – Fire Pumps\n- 21 12 00 – Standpipes\n- 21 13 00 – Sprinkler Systems\n\n**Related Sections to Check:**\n- 22 11 16 – Domestic water (FDC tie-ins)\n- 26 24 00 – Switchboards (fire pump power)\n- 28 31 00 – Fire Alarm (integration)\n\n## Key Codes & Standards\n\n- **NFPA 13** – Sprinkler Systems\n- **NFPA 14** – Standpipes and Hose Systems\n- **NFPA 20** – Fire Pumps\n- **NFPA 25** – Inspection, Testing, Maintenance\n- **NFPA 72** – Fire Alarm (integration)\n- **NYC Building Code Chapter 9** – Fire Protection (if NYC)\n- **Local AHJ requirements**\n\n## Takeoff Methodology\n\n### 1. System Identification\n- Identify all fire protection systems on project\n- Classify: Wet sprinkler, dry sprinkler, preaction, deluge, standpipe, clean agent\n- Note: Combined vs. separate systems\n\n### 2. Riser & Standpipe Takeoff\n- Count risers and standpipes\n- Measure heights (floor-to-floor × number of floors)\n- Identify pipe sizes from riser diagrams\n- Note: Fire department connections (FDC) locations and types\n- Check: Pressure zones, PRVs required\n\n### 3. Fire Pump Analysis\n- Pump type: Horizontal, vertical, in-line\n- Pump size: GPM and PSI\n- Driver: Electric or diesel\n- Controller type\n- Jockey pump included?\n\n### 4. Sprinkler Head Count\n- Count by type: Pendant, upright, sidewall, concealed\n- Note temperature ratings\n- Coverage areas vs. head counts\n- Special heads: ESFR, extended coverage, residential\n\n### 5. Piping Takeoff\n- Main sizes (typically 4\", 6\", 8\")\n- Branch line sizes (typically 1\", 1.25\", 1.5\", 2\")\n- Measure runs from drawings (scale)\n- Count fittings by size\n- Note materials: Black steel, CPVC, grooved, threaded\n\n### 6. Valves & Devices\n- OS&Y valves\n- Butterfly valves\n- Check valves\n- Flow switches\n- Tamper switches\n- Pressure gauges\n- Inspector's test connections\n\n### 7. Hangers & Supports\n- Calculate based on pipe runs (typically every 10-12 ft)\n- Seismic bracing requirements\n- Trapeze vs. individual hangers\n\n### 8. Penetrations & Firestopping\n- Count floor/wall penetrations\n- Firestopping at rated assemblies\n\n## What You Flag\n\n### ⚠️ Conflicts\n- Sprinkler heads in conflict with HVAC diffusers\n- Pipe routing conflicts with ductwork\n- Structural interference with mains\n\n### ❓ RFI Candidates\n- Missing riser diagrams\n- Unclear PRV requirements\n- Hydraulic calc responsibility\n- Seismic bracing not detailed\n- FDC location not shown\n\n### 💰 Cost Drivers\n- Fire pump (major cost item)\n- System type (dry > wet)\n- Height (standpipe pressure zones)\n- Seismic requirements\n- Special hazard suppression\n\n### 📋 Coordination Items\n- Fire alarm integration points\n- Electrical power for fire pump\n- Plumbing tie-in for domestic water\n- Structural penetrations\n\n## Output Format\n\n```markdown\n## Fire Protection Takeoff — [Project Name]\n\n### System Summary\n| System | Type | Zones/Risers | Notes |\n|--------|------|--------------|-------|\n\n### Fire Pump (if applicable)\n- Type: \n- Capacity: ___ GPM @ ___ PSI\n- Driver: Electric / Diesel\n- Controller: \n- Jockey Pump: Yes / No\n\n### Standpipes\n| Standpipe ID | Type | Height | Size | Notes |\n|--------------|------|--------|------|-------|\n\n### Sprinkler Systems\n| Zone | Type | Heads | Coverage SF | Head Type |\n|------|------|-------|-------------|-----------|\n\n### Piping Summary\n| Size | Linear Feet | Material | Notes |\n|------|-------------|----------|-------|\n\n### Valves & Devices\n| Item | Quantity | Size | Notes |\n|------|----------|------|-------|\n\n### Hangers & Supports\n- Main hangers: ___\n- Branch hangers: ___\n- Seismic braces: ___\n\n### Flags & Issues\n#### ⚠️ Conflicts\n- \n\n#### ❓ RFIs Needed\n- \n\n#### 💰 Cost Drivers\n- \n\n#### 🔗 Coordination Required\n- \n\n### Confidence Assessment\n- Overall: High / Medium / Low\n- Notes: \n```\n\n## Common Gotchas\n\n1. **Hydraulic calcs** – Who's responsible? Usually contractor, but verify.\n2. **Seismic** – Often spec'd but not detailed on drawings.\n3. **Ceiling type** – Concealed heads for finished ceilings add cost.\n4. **Access panels** – Needed above concealed heads.\n5. **Standpipe class** – Class I, II, or III affects cabinet requirements.\n6. **PRVs** – Required above certain heights; often missed.\n7. **FDC** – Location, type, and Siamese connection count.\n8. **Antifreeze** – Dry systems in cold areas may need glycol.\n9. **Escutcheons** – Match ceiling type/color.\n10. **Floor control valves** – Required per floor in standpipes.\n\n## Memory Injection Point\n\n<!-- MEMORY_START -->\n{Inject from experts/memory/fire-protection.md}\n<!-- MEMORY_END -->\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138916706}}
{"type":"message","id":"cea78716","parentId":"6d367ac9","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:15:16.729Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01Pj3H7B5bb6Hgn7HW6tWovX","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 468\ndrwxrwxr-x. 2 ec2-user ec2-user  16384 Feb  3 17:11 .\ndrwxrwxr-x. 4 ec2-user ec2-user    169 Feb  3 17:12 ..\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  28172 Feb  3 17:09 IFB-Part1.txt\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  54387 Feb  3 17:09 Section-AB-Revised.txt\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user 211523 Feb  3 17:10 abatement-spec.txt\n-rw-r--r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user   6282 Feb  3 17:11 master-index.json\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  39152 Feb  3 17:10 spec-21-12-00-standpipes.txt\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  40032 Feb  3 17:10 spec-21-30-00-fire-pumps.txt\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  72292 Feb  3 17:10 spec-div21-part1.txt"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":19,"aggregated":"total 468\ndrwxrwxr-x. 2 ec2-user ec2-user  16384 Feb  3 17:11 .\ndrwxrwxr-x. 4 ec2-user ec2-user    169 Feb  3 17:12 ..\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  28172 Feb  3 17:09 IFB-Part1.txt\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  54387 Feb  3 17:09 Section-AB-Revised.txt\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user 211523 Feb  3 17:10 abatement-spec.txt\n-rw-r--r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user   6282 Feb  3 17:11 master-index.json\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  39152 Feb  3 17:10 spec-21-12-00-standpipes.txt\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  40032 Feb  3 17:10 spec-21-30-00-fire-pumps.txt\n-rw-rw-r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  72292 Feb  3 17:10 spec-div21-part1.txt","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138916727}}
{"type":"message","id":"f0a3ac51","parentId":"cea78716","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:15:23.814Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! I have all the source materials. Now let me analyze the discrepancies:\n\nCRITICAL DISCREPANCY - Standpipe Count:\n- Alpha (Bid-First): 7 standpipes (1 base + 6 alternates)\n- Beta (Doc-First): 6 standpipes (1 base + 5 alternates)\n\nLet me read the extracted specs to resolve this. I need to dig into the standpipe spec and the alternates section to determine the actual count.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Good. I see the critical discrepancy: **Alpha found 7 standpipes**, **Beta found 6 standpipes**. Let me dig into the source documents to resolve this."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GUncstgX8mQFSFKbfXZGQu","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/extracted/spec-21-12-00-standpipes.txt"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01VHiFjuSYMZepwMqLKZhKz2","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/extracted/Section-AB-Revised.txt"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_019PWn4eJYs4wMNVw7sYVhdL","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/bellevue-standpipe/extracted/master-index.json"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":8,"output":390,"cacheRead":10521,"cacheWrite":16615,"totalTokens":27534,"cost":{"input":0.00004,"output":0.00975,"cacheRead":0.0052604999999999996,"cacheWrite":0.10384375,"total":0.11889424999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770138916729}}
{"type":"message","id":"a2d684cc","parentId":"f0a3ac51","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:15:23.827Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01GUncstgX8mQFSFKbfXZGQu","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\fSECTION 21 12 00\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n1.01\n\nSUMMARY\n\nA.\n\nSection includes entire standpipe system from fire department connection to fire hose\nconnection and the following:\n1.\nComplete wet fire standpipe system.\n2.\nRoof manifold.\n3.\nAngle Hose Valves.\n4.\nFire Hose and Nozzles\n5.\nAccessories for Valves and Hoses.\n6.\nHose Valve Cabinets\n7.\nDetention Locked Hose Valve Cabinets\n8.\nPainting and Identification of piping.\n9.\nValve Supervisory Switches\n\nB.\n\nRelated Sections:\n1.\nDivision 08 - Access Doors and Frames: Product requirements for access doors\nfor placement by this section.\n2.\nDivision 09 - Painting and Coating: Product and execution requirements for\npainting specified by this section.\n3.\nSection 21 05 00 - Common Work Results for Fire Suppression: Product and\nexecution requirements for pipe, fittings, valves, hangers, supports, identification\nand painting for placement by this section.\n4.\nSection 21 05 03 - Pipes Tubes for Fire-Suppression Piping and Equipment:\nProduct requirements for piping for placement by this section.\n5.\nSection 21 05 05 - Hangers and Supports for Fire-Suppression Piping and\nEquipment: Product requirements for pipe hangers and supports and firestopping\nfor placement by this section.\n6.\nSection 21 13 13 - Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems: Product requirements for wet\nsprinkler piping for placement by this section.\n\n1.02\n\nREFERENCES\n\nA.\n\nFM Global:\n1.\nFM - Approval Guide, A Guide to Equipment, Materials & Services Approved\nBy Factory Mutual Research For Property Conservation.\n\nB.\n\nNational Fire Protection Association:\n1.\nNFPA 14 - Standard for the Installation of Standpipe, Private Hydrants and Hose\nSystems.\n\n1.03\nA.\n\nSUBMITTALS\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures:\nSubmittal procedures.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fB.\n\nShop Drawings: Indicate supports, components, accessories and sizes.\n\nC.\n\nProduct Data: Submit manufacturer's catalog sheet for equipment indicating rough-in\nsize, finish, and accessories.\n\nD.\n\nField Test Reports: Indicate compliance with specified performance.\n\nE.\n\nManufacturer's Installation Instructions: Submit with product data.\n\nF.\n\nManufacturer's Certificate: Certify products meet or exceed specified requirements.\n\n1.04\n\nCLOSEOUT SUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Closeout procedures.\n\nB.\n\nOperation and Maintenance Data: Submit servicing requirements and test schedule.\n\n1.05\n\nQUALITY ASSURANCE\n\nA.\n\nPerform Work in accordance with NYCBC.\n\nB.\n\nMaintain one (1) copy of each document on site.\n\n1.06\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this\nsection with minimum three (3) years documented experience.\n\nB.\n\nInstaller: Company specializing in performing Work of this section with minimum three\n(3) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\n1.07\n\nDELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\nRequirements for transporting, handling, storing, and protecting products.\n\nB.\n\nDeliver and store products in shipping packaging until installation.\n\n1.08\n\nWARRANTY\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Product warranties and product bonds.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish five-year manufacturer warranty for standpipes and valves.\n\n1.09\n\nEXTRA MATERIALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Spare parts and maintenance products.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish two (2) hose nozzles and hoses.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 2\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n2.01\nA.\n2.02\nA.\n\n2.03\n\nGENERAL\nAll threads are to conform to NYC Fire Department requirements.\nPIPE ESCUTCHEONS\nPipe escutcheons shall have an inside diameter closely fitting pipe outside diameter or\noutside of pipe insulation where pipe is insulated. Select outside diameter of\nescutcheon to completely cover pipe penetration hole in floors, walls, or ceilings; and\npipe sleeve extension, if any. Escutcheons shall be cast or sheet brass, solid or splithinged, with brass set screw. Provide chrome finish for occupied areas exposed to\nview.\nPIPE SLEEVES\n\nA.\n\nProvide pipe sleeves of one of the following. Pipe sleeve must be appropriate type and\nthickness for the UL firestopping assembly selected:\n1.\nSheet-Metal: Fabricate from galvanized sheet metal; round tube closed with\nsnaplock joint, welded spiral seams, or welded longitudinal joint. Fabricate from\nthe following gauges: 3\" and smaller, 20 gage minimum; 4\" to 6\", 16 gage; over\n6\", 14 gage minimum.\n2.\nSteel-Pipe: Fabricate from Schedule 40 galvanized steel pipe; remove burrs.\n3.\nIron-Pipe: Fabricate from cast-iron or ductile-iron pipe; remove burrs.\n4.\nFirestop penetration materials for sealing sleeves shall be listed by Underwriters\nLaboratories and if not listed have MEA or OTCR approval. The materials shall\nbe as specified in Section 07 27 0. For pipes passing through fire-rated floor,\ncast-in place firestop device with Underwriters Laboratories listing, and if not\nlisted have MEA or OTCR approval, is permitted as an acceptable sleeve\nalternative to a metallic sleeve with firestopping material. The cast-in place\ndevice is a one-step firestopping process that does not require additional firestop\npenetration materials for sealing the sleeves. The device shall be installed where\nrequired for sleeving purposes. The cast-in place firestop device shall not be used\nfor wall applications.\n\nB.\n\nMaterials for sealing space between each pipe and sleeve through non-rated interior\nwalls shall consist of mineral wool and sealant.\n\n2.04\n\nFIRE HOSE VALVES AND CABINETS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nPotter Roemer\n2.\nWSA Inc.\n3.\nCroker.\n\nB.\n\nCabinet: Suitable for 2-1/2” fire department valve and 1-1/2” hose rack assembly,\nrecessed, stainless steel 304 door with 20 gauge steel frame, dual horizontal panel, red\npowder coat finish, fire rated tub insulated with Firespan 90 tested by UL and rated to\nASTM E814. Similar to Croker 1410 Series Fire-Rated hose cabinet, rated to 2 hours.\n\nC.\n\nLocked Detention Cabinets: Constructed for maximum security facilities with 12 gauge\ncold rolled steel. Mitered and ground smooth corners. Cabinet shall be powder coated\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 3\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fwith thermally-fused polyester red finish. Heavy-duty continuous hinge. Door shall be\nflush solid metal with security-type lock. Recessed cabinet. Potter Roemer model#\nDC1810-F.\nD.\n\nHose Connection Valve: Angle type; brass finish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 11/2 inch reducer, thread to match fire department hardware, with threaded cap and chain\nof brass finish. Hose valve shall conform to FDNY standards. Valves shall be similar\nto Potter Roemer Fig. 4065 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5015. Cap with chain shall be similar\nto Potter Roemer 4625 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5713. Threads shall be to NYC Fire\ndepartment specifications.\n\nE.\n\nHose Rack Assembly:\n1.\nSimilar to Croker Model 3307 Style N.\n2.\nUL 47, semiautomatic hose stations. Include brass rack nipple, hose rack, and\nthe following:\na.\nValve: UL 668, brass or bronze, 300-psig minimum pressure rating, 90degree-angle-pattern hose valve with female NPS inlet and outlet, brass\nfinish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 1-1/2 inch reducer, thread to\nmatch fire department hardware. Valve Operation: Nonadjustable type,\nunless pressure-regulating type is indicated. Hose Valve and Trim Finish:\nPolished chrome-plated.\nb.\nHose Rack: Steel; Semi-automatic swinging type with pins for folding\nhose and water stop. Finish: Red enamel.\nc.\nHose: NFPA 1961 and UL 219, lined fire hose, 1-1/2 inch diameter, 125\nfeet long, of polyurethane lined synthetic hose; mildew and rot-resistant.\nd.\nNozzle: UL 401, brass, combination fog, straight stream, and adjustable\nshut-off. Finish: polished brass.\ne.\nDrain Valves: UL 1726.\n\nF.\n\nPressure Restricting Hose Valve:\n1.\nPressure-Restricting Hose Valve Class: NPS 2-1/2” and 1-1/2”, brass, adjustable\nsimilar to Croker model 5560 set at 100 psi.\n\n2.05\nA.\n\nFIRE DEPARTMENT LOBBY HOSE CABINET\nFire Department Lobby Hose Cabinet:\n1.\nCabinet, with built-in storage shelf for storing below listed equipment, shall be\nrecessed type, 20-gage steel body and baked white polyester finish inside.\nExposed trim and door shall be 18-gage, with continuous steel hinge (brass pin).\nCabinet door shall have duo-panel wire inserted clear glass. Door shall be hinged\nright or left as required with lock and key in a key cabinet. Cabinet shall be\nPotter Roemer 1302 or Croker Corp. Fig. 2190. The cabinet shall be labeled “For\nFire Department Use Only”. Final size dependent on amount of material to be\nplaced in cabinet.\na.\nClass I standpipe requires the installation of a storage cabinet on the main\nentrance floor. Where one standpipe riser is installed in the building, the\ncabinet shall contain at least one fog nozzle, one 1½” spanner wrench, one\n2½” wrench, one 2½”x 1.5” non-swivel reducing coupling, and 125’ of\n1½” hose. Also provide one pressure restricting device to limit static and\nresidual pressures at the outlet of the hose connection to 100 psi. For\nbuildings over 10 stories, provide another cabinet at the tenth floor (and\nevery ten floors thereafter). Where two or more standpipe risers are\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 4\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fb.\nB.\n\n2.06\n\ninstalled in the building, at least two of the required items of equipment\nlisted herein shall be provided.\nThe equipment specified for the Lobby Storage Cabinet shall be of one\nmanufacturer for each complete unit.\n\nLobby Key Storage Cabinet:\n1.\nThe key to the “Lobby Storage Cabinet” shall be kept in a locked “Key Storage\nCabinet”, openable only by a Fire Department city wide standard key. The\ncabinet shall be labeled “For Fire Department Use Only”. A metal sign stating\nwhere the storage cabinet is located shall be placed in each stair enclosure on the\nmain entrance and on each floor. The cabinet shall hold a key for the lobby\nstorage cabinet. Cabinet installation requires 5”x5”x3” wall opening. Cabinet\nshall be Potter Roemer model #1950 NYFD Yale lock #SYA1, or Croker Fig.\n2928 or Fig. 2920.\nFIRE DEPARTMENT CONNECTION\n\nA.\n\nFlush type shall be of the size indicated on drawings. Fire Department connections shall\nbe polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves and cast iron plugs painted\nyellow with brass chain and with polished plate lettered “COMBINATION\nSTANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter inscription shall be either an\nintegral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate securely fastened to or above the\nFire Department connection. Flush type shall be Potter Roemer Fig. 5020G Series\n(THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig. 6030 Series (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads\nshall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\nB.\n\nExposed type shall be of the size indicated on the drawings. Fire Department\nconnections shall be polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves, pin lug\nswivels, plugs and chains painted yellow and with polished brass wall plate lettered\n“COMBINATION STANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter\ninscription shall be either an integral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate\nsecurely fastened to or above the Fire Department connection. Expose type shall be\nPotter- Roemer, Fig. 5750 Series (THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig 6430\nSeries (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads shall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\nC.\n\nOutlets: Two-way with fire department thread size. Threaded dust-cap and chain of\nmatching material and finish.\n\nD.\n\nDrain: 3/4 inch automatic drip pipe to outside or connected to drain via indirect drain.\n\nE.\n\nWhere a fence encloses a portion of the building containing a Fire Department\nconnection, Contractor shall provide and secure to the fence directly opposite the Fire\nDepartment connection a steel sign containing the following wording: \"F.D. Fire\nDepartment Connection located...Feet behind Sign.\" Sign shall be finished in porcelain\nenamel with 1-inch red letters on white background.\n\n2.07\n\nROOF MANIFOLD FIRE DEPARTMENT OUTLET CONNECTION:\n\nA.\n\nStyle: Free standing, angle inlet. Cast brass body.\n\nB.\n\nConnections: 6-inch female NPT inlet and four (4) 2-1/2-inch male NPT outlets.\n\nC.\n\nRoof outlet shall be fitted with three cast brass valves.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 5\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\f2.08\n\nPRESSURE GAUGES\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nTerice Model 600C\n2.\nWeksler Model Regal\n3.\nAGF Manufacturing Co.\n4.\nAMETEK, Inc.; U.S. Gauge.\n5.\nDresser Equipment Group; Instrument Div.\n\nB.\n\nDescription: UL 393, 4-1/2-inch- diameter, dial pressure gage with range of -10 to 300\npsig minimum. Cast brass, type ‘L’ case, glass covered, and phosphor bronze bourdon\ntype tube. Include caption \"WATER\" on dial face.\n\n2.09\nA.\n2.10\nA.\n\n2.11\n\nAUTOMATIC BALL DRIP\nAutomatic Ball Drip shall be 3/4\" Potter-Roemer Fig. 5982 or Croker Corp. Fig. 6781.\nLADDERS\nProvide permanent heavy steel ladders to provide access to valves in accordance with\nthe code requirements. Ladders shall be of width and height required, shall be made of\nheavy steel bars and heavy rungs and shall be permanently fastened at location. Where\nthe shut-off valve adjacent to the sprinkler alarm valve is located higher than 6' above\nthe floor, ladder shall be provided where directed.\nPAINTING\n\nA.\n\nPaints used on dedicated piping to combination sprinkler and standpipe shall not:\n1.\nExceed the VOC content limits established in the Green Seal Standard GS-11\nPaints, first edition, May 20, 1993.\n2.\nExceed the VOC content limit of 250 g/L established in the Green Seal Standard\nGC-03, Anti-Corrosive paints, second edition, January 7, 1997.\n\nB.\n\nProvide colors indicated in Paragraph 3.04\n1.\nFirst (1st) coat – Alkyd Vinyl Acrylic – Latex Primer – 1.2 Mills DFT\n2.\nSecond (2nd) coat – Semi-Gloss Vinyl Acrylic Latex – Enamel – 1.3 Mills DFT\n\n2.12\n\nVALVE SUPERVISORY SWITCHES\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nPotter Electric Signal Co. Model OSYSU-2\n2.\nFire-Lite Alarms, Inc.; a Honeywell company.\n3.\nKennedy Valve; a division of McWane, Inc.\n4.\nSystem Sensor; a Honeywell company.\n\nB.\n\nStandard: UL 346.\n\nC.\n\nType: Electrically supervised.\n\nD.\n\nComponents: Single-pole, double-throw switch with normally closed contacts.\n\nE.\n\nDesign: Signals that controlled valve is in other than fully open position.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 6\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fF.\n\nLocate on each valve as designated on the drawings. Switches shall be mounted so not\nto interfere with the normal operation of the valve and shall be adjusted to operate\nwithin two revolutions of the valve control or when the stem has moved no more than\none-fifth of the distance from its normal position. The switch mechanism shall be\ncontained in a weatherproof die-cast aluminum housing which shall provide 3/4” tapped\nconduit entrance and incorporate the necessary facilities for attachment to the valve.\nSwitch housings shall be finished in red baked enamel.\n\nPART 3 - EXECUTION\n3.01\n\nEXAMINATION\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Administrative\nRequirements: Coordination and project conditions.\n\nB.\n\nVerify blocking in place for cabinet installation.\n\n3.02\n\nINSTALLATION\n\nA.\n\nInstall in accordance with NFPA 14.\n\nB.\n\nInstall cabinets plumb and level. Secure to adjacent surfaces. Establish top of cabinet\n(inside horizontal) surface 66 inches above finished floor.\n\nC.\n\nInstall hose station valve in cabinet at 60 inches above floor.\n\nD.\n\nConnect standpipe system to water source separate from domestic water connection.\n\nE.\n\nWhere static pressure exceeds 100 psi at any hose station, furnish pressure orifice disc\nin discharge of hose station valve to prevent pressure on hose exceeding 90 psi.\n\nF.\n\nInstall three-way fire department outlet on roof.\n\n3.03\n\nFIELD QUALITY CONTROL\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Quality Requirements,\nand Execution and Closeout Requirements: Field inspecting, testing, adjusting and\nbalancing.\n\nB.\n\nTest entire system in accordance with NFPA 14.\n\nC.\n\nRequire test be witnessed by Fire Marshall, Authority having jurisdiction and Owner's\ninsurance underwriter.\n\n3.04\nA.\n\nTESTING\nHydrostatic Testing: After flushing system, test standpipe piping hydrostatically, for\nperiod of 2 hour, at not less than 300 psi or 50 psi in excess of the system working\npressure, whichever is greater. Check system for leakage of joints. The test pressure\nshall be read from a gage located at the low point of each system or zone being tested.\n1.\nRepair or replace piping system as required to eliminate leakage.\n2.\nTest the entire fire protection installation, including fire alarm system, in\naccordance with the requirements of the NYC Fire Code and give at least 2 days\nadvance notice in writing of tests and inspections to the Construction Inspection\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 7\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fDivision and the Authority. Tests shall be conducted in the presence of the any\npublic authority having jurisdiction. All tests shall be performed as part of this\ncontract.\n3.05\n\nFIELD PAINTING\n\nA.\n\nProtect sprinkler heads during painting with small paper bags. Painting of sprinkler/ fire\nstandpipe piping, hangers, and all other items and accessories shall conform to the code\nrequirements.\n\nB.\n\nPaint standpipes in accordance with Specification Section 21 05 00.\n\n3.06\n\nCLEANING\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Final cleaning.\n\nB.\n\nFlush entire system of foreign matter.\n\nEND OF SECTION 21 12 00\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 8\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fSECTION 21 13 13\nWET-PIPE SPRINKLER SYSTEMS\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n1.01\n\nSUMMARY\n\nA.\n\nSection includes:\n1.\nWet-pipe sprinkler system.\n2.\nSystem design.\n3.\nInstallation and certification.\n\nB.\n\nRelated Sections:\n1.\nDivision 26 - Wiring Connections: Execution requirements for electric\nconnections to equipment specified by this section.\n\n1.02\nA.\n\n1.03\n\nREFERENCES\nNational Fire Protection Association:\n1.\nNFPA 13 - Installation of Sprinkler Systems.\n2.\nFactory Mutual Global.\nSYSTEM DESCRIPTION\n\nA.\n\nSystem to provide coverage for entire building areas noted in Drawing Schedule.\n\nB.\n\nProvide hydraulically designed system to NFPA 13 light hazard and ordinary hazard,\nGroup 1 occupancy requirements.\n\nC.\n\nInterface system building fire alarm system.\n\nD.\n\nProvide fire department connections as indicated on Drawings.\n\n1.04\n\nSUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures:\nSubmittal procedures.\n\nB.\n\nShop Drawings: Indicate layout of finished ceiling areas indicating sprinkler locations\ncoordinated with ceiling installation. Indicate detailed pipe layout, hangers and\nsupports, sprinklers, components and accessories. Indicate system controls. Submit\nhydrant flow test, hydraulic calculations and shop drawings. Signed and sealed by\nprofessional engineer licensed in the State of New York.\n\nC.\n\nProduct Data: Submit data on sprinklers, valves, and specialties, including\nmanufacturers catalog information. Submit performance ratings, rough-in details,\nweights, support requirements, and piping connections.\n\nD.\n\nSamples: Submit two (2) of each style of sprinkler specified.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nWET-PIPE SPRINKLER SYSTEMS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 13 13 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fE.\n\nDesign Data: Submit design calculations; signed and sealed by professional engineer\nlicensed in the State of New York.\n\nF.\n\nManufacturer's Certificate: Certify products meet or exceed specified requirements.\n\n1.05\n\nCLOSEOUT SUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Closeout procedures.\n\nB.\n\nProject Record Documents: Record actual locations of sprinklers and deviations of\npiping from drawings. Indicate drain and test locations.\n\nC.\n\nOperation and Maintenance Data: Submit components of system, servicing\nrequirements, record drawings, inspection data, replacement part numbers and\navailability, and location and numbers of service depot.\n\n1.06\n\nQUALITY ASSURANCE\n\nA.\n\nPerform Work in accordance with NYCBC and NFPA 13 - 2016 as amended by\nAppendix Q.\n\nB.\n\nMaintain one (1) copy of each document on site.\n\nC.\n\nInstall sprinkler/fire standpipe systems in accordance with local regulations of the NYC\nFire Department.\n\nD.\n\nComply with local Fire Department regulations for sizes, threading and arrangement of\nconnections for fire department equipment to Fire Department connections.\n\nE.\n\nAll gauges, instruments and test devices shall be provided with a certificate of\ncalibration and calibration curve or letter indicating that a minimum of five (5) test\npoints have been calibrated. The certificate and letter must show the date of last\ncalibration. The calibration date must be within a year of the testing date.\n\n1.07\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this\nsection with minimum three (3) years documented experience.\n\nB.\n\nInstaller: Company specializing in performing Work of this section with minimum three\n(3) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\nC.\n\nDesign system under direct supervision of Professional Engineer experienced in design\nof this Work and licensed in the State of New York.\n\n1.08\n\nDELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\nProduct storage and handling requirements.\n\nB.\n\nStore products in shipping containers until installation.\n\nC.\n\nFurnish piping with temporary inlet and outlet caps until installation.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nWET-PIPE SPRINKLER SYSTEMS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 13 13 - 2\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\f1.09\n\nWARRANTY\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Product warranties and product bonds.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish five-year manufacturer warranty.\n\n1.10\n\nEXTRA MATERIALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Spare parts and maintenance products.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish extra sprinklers under provisions of NFPA 13.\n\nC.\n\nFurnish suitable wrenches for each sprinkler type.\n\nD.\n\nFurnish metal storage cabinet.\n\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n2.01\n\nAUTOMATIC SPRINKLERS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nReliable Automatic Sprinkler Corp.\n2.\nViking Sprinkler Corp.\n3.\nGrinnell\n\nB.\n\nSuspended and Gypsum Board Ceiling Type:\n1.\nType: Concealed pendant type with matching push on cover plate.\n2.\nFinish: Specified by Architect.\n3.\nEscutcheon Plate Finish: Specified by Architect.\n4.\nFusible Link: Glass bulb type temperature rated for specific area hazard.\n\nC.\n\nExposed Area Type:\n1.\nType: Standard upright type with guard.\n2.\nFinish: Brass.\n3.\nFusible Link: Glass bulb type temperature rated for specific area hazard.\n\nD.\n\nSidewall Type:\n1.\nType: Semi-recessed horizontal side wall type with matching push on\nescutcheon plate and guard.\n2.\nFinish: Enamel, color white.\n3.\nEscutcheon Plate Finish: Enamel, color white.\n4.\nFusible Link: Glass bulb type temperature rated for specific area hazard.\n\nE.\n\nGuards: Finish to match sprinkler finish.\n\n2.02\n\nALARM DEVICES\n\nA.\n\nAlarm-device types shall match piping and equipment connections.\n\nB.\n\nWater-Flow Indicators:\n1.\nPotter Electric Signal Co. Model VSR-F.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nWET-PIPE SPRINKLER SYSTEMS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 13 13 - 3\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\f2.\n3.\n4.\n\n5.\n6.\n7.\nC.\n\nStandard: UL 346.\nWater-Flow Detector: Electrically supervised.\nComponents: Two single-pole, double-throw circuit switches for isolated alarm\nand auxiliary contacts, 7 A, 125-V ac and 0.25 A, 24-V dc; complete with\nfactory-set, field-adjustable retard element to prevent false signals and\ntamperproof cover that sends signal if removed.\nType: Paddle operated.\nPressure Rating: 250 psig.\nDesign Installation: Horizontal or vertical.\n\nValve Supervisory Switches:\n1.\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by\none of the following:\na.\nPotter Electric Signal Co. Model OSYSU-2\nb.\nFire-Lite Alarms, Inc.; a Honeywell company.\nc.\nKennedy Valve; a division of McWane, Inc.\nd.\nSystem Sensor; a Honeywell company.\n2.\nStandard: UL 346.\n3.\nType: Electrically supervised.\n4.\nComponents: Single-pole, double-throw switch with normally closed contacts.\n5.\nDesign: Signals that controlled valve is in other than fully open position.\n6.\nLocate on each valve as designated on the drawings. Switches shall be mounted\nso not to interfere with the normal operation of the valve and shall be adjusted to\noperate within two revolutions of the valve control or when the stem has moved\nno more than one-fifth of the distance from its normal position. The switch\nmechanism shall be contained in a weatherproof die-cast aluminum housing\nwhich shall provide 3/4” tapped conduit entrance and incorporate the necessary\nfacilities for attachment to the valve. Switch housings shall be finished in red\nbaked enamel.\n\nPART 3 - EXECUTION\n3.01\nA.\n\n3.02\n\nGENERAL\nInformation included in this specification and of various agency requirements are given\nas a guide only. The contract documents do not relieve Contractor’s responsibility to\nprovide all work and equipment necessary to complete the installation in accordance\nwith all requirements.\nINSTALLATION\n\nA.\n\nInstall in accordance with NFPA 13.\n\nB.\n\nNo pipes or other apparatus shall be installed so as to interfere in any way with the full\nswing of the doors. The arrangement, positions and connections of pipes, drains,\nvalves, etc., shown on the drawings, shall be taken as a close approximation and while\nthey shall be followed as closely as possible, the right is reserved by the architect to\nchange the locations to accommodate any conditions which may arise during the\nprogress of the work without additional compensation to this contractor for such\nchanges, provided that the changes are requested to the installation of this work.\n\nC.\n\nAll piping shall drain back to the risers or be provided with drain valves. Special\nprecautions must be taken to avoid electrical work and ventilation ducts and no piping\nshall pass below lighting fixtures in luminous ceilings or under skylights.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nWET-PIPE SPRINKLER SYSTEMS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 13 13 - 4\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fD.\n\nAll piping shall be unexposed except in no-ceiling areas. Where required, heads shall\nbe located below ducts. Diffusers and lighting fixtures take preference in room layout.\n\nE.\n\nIn areas with restricted head room, heads and piping shall be tight to ceilings and\nprovided with guards.\n\nF.\n\nNo heads shall be nearer than 6 inches to a ceiling support, and where 12” x 12”, 24” x\n24” or 24” x 48” ceiling panels are used, the heads shall be located in the center of the\npanel.\n\nG.\n\nInstall sprinkler heads in all areas on a true axis line in both directions with a maximum\ndeviation from the axis of 1/2” plus or minus. In acoustical tile ceilings, sprinkler heads\nshall be located on center of tile. At the completion of the installation, remove and\nreinstall any heads found to exceed the above mentioned tolerances.\n\nH.\n\nInstall guards on sprinklers as indicated on Drawings or as verified in field as requiring\na guard.\n\nI.\n\nHydrostatically test entire system in accordance with NFPA 13.\n\nJ.\n\nRequire test be witnessed by Fire Authority having jurisdiction and Engineer’s\nrepresentative.\n\nK.\n\nInstall automatic (ball drip) drain valve at each check valve for fire-department\nconnection, to drain piping between fire-department connection and check valve.\nInstall drain piping to and spill over floor drain or to outside building.\n\nL.\n\nInstall pressure gages on riser or feed main, at each sprinkler test connection, and at top\nof each standpipe. Include pressure gages with connection not less than NPS 1/4 and\nwith soft metal seated globe valve, arranged for draining pipe between gage and valve.\nInstall gages to permit removal, and install where they will not be subject to freezing.\n\nM.\n\nInstall escutcheons for piping penetrations of walls, ceilings, and floors.\n\n3.03\n\nSPRINKLER COVERAGE\n\nA.\n\nFor determination of sprinkler systems, spacing and sizing, the following coverage\nratings as listed in NFPA 13 and as listed by the insurance company for this project\nshall be followed. Also, comply with local authorities’ requirements.\n\nB.\n\nProvide sprinklers where shown on the drawings.\n\nC.\n\nHydraulically Calculated System: The system shall be hydraulically designed to\nprovide a density based on NFPA requirements and the requirements of the insurance\ncompany and the local authorities.\nArea\nGeneral Public Areas,\nOffices\nStorage rooms\nMechanical spaces.\n\nD.\n\nHazard\nClassification\nLight\n\nDensity\nGPM/Sq.Ft.\n0.10\n\nArea of\nApplication\n1500\n\nOrdinary I\n\n0.15\n\n1500\n\nLight Hazard Coverage: 225 square feet per sprinkler head.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nWET-PIPE SPRINKLER SYSTEMS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 13 13 - 5\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fE.\n\nOrdinary Hazard Coverage: 130 square feet per sprinkler head.\n\nF.\n\nFloor Openings: A curtain of sprinkler heads on 6’-0” centers shall be provided to\nencircle the floor opening at the draft curtain to conform to NFPA 13, 4-4.8.2.3 and\n85A4-4.8.2.3.\n\n3.04\n\nDRAINS AND TEST PIPES\n\nA.\n\nProvide drains at base of riser, valved sections inside building, and other locations\nindicated or requiring same for complete drainage of systems. Siamese drains shall be\nequipped with automatic ball drips. Other drains shall be valves and/or plugs as\nindicated and/or required. Pipe drains to location as required.\n\nB.\n\nTest pipes shall be valved and piped to discharge through proper orifice at approved\nlocations.\n\nC.\n\nInstall buried shut-off valves in valve box.\n\nD.\n\nApproved double check valve back-flow preventer assembly installed at sprinkler\nsystem water source connection by the Plumbing Contractor.\n\nE.\n\nLocate fire department connection with sufficient clearance from walls, obstructions, or\nadjacent Siamese connectors to allow full swing of fire department wrench handle.\nInstall pipe bollards to protect from possible damage.\n\nF.\n\nPlace pipe runs to minimize obstruction to other work.\n\nG.\n\nInstall piping in concealed spaces above finished ceilings.\n\nH.\n\nHydrostatically test entire system in accordance with NFPA 13 and New York City\nBuilding Code Appendix Q.\n\nI.\n\nRequire test be witnessed by special inspector.\n\n3.05\nA.\n3.06\n\nINTERFACE WITH OTHER PRODUCTS\nVerify signal devices are installed and connected to fire alarm system.\nCLEANING\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Final cleaning.\n\nB.\n\nFlush entire piping system of foreign matter.\n\nC.\n\nApply masking tape or paper cover to protect concealed sprinklers, cover plates, and\nsprinkler escutcheons not receiving field paint finish. Remove after painting. Replace\npainted sprinklers with new.\n\n3.07\nA.\n\nPAINTING\nProtect sprinkler heads during painting with small paper bags. Apply masking tape or\npaper cover to protect concealed sprinklers, cover plates, and sprinkler escutcheons not\nreceiving field paint finish. Remove after painting. Painting of sprinkler/ fire standpipe\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nWET-PIPE SPRINKLER SYSTEMS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 13 13 - 6\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fpiping, hangers, and all other items and accessories shall conform to the code\nrequirements.\nB.\n\nPaint sprinkler mains and combination standpipe/sprinkler mains in accordance with\nSpecification Section 21 05 00.\n\nEND OF SECTION 21 13 13\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nWET-PIPE SPRINKLER SYSTEMS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 13 13 - 7\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fSECTION 21 30 00\nFIRE PUMPS\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n1.01\n\nSUMMARY\n\nA.\n\nSection includes\n1.\nFire pump package and motor.\n2.\nControllers for electric fire pumps.\n3.\nElectric jockey pump.\n4.\nControllers for pressure-maintenance pumps.\n5.\nFire-pump accessories and specialties\n6.\nFlowmeter Systems\n\nB.\n\nRelated Sections:\n1.\nSection 210500 - Common Work Results for Fire Suppression: Product\nrequirements for Fire piping placement by this section.\n2.\nSection 21 05 48 - Noise and Vibration Controls for Fire-Suppression Piping and\nEquipment: Product requirements for pump isolators for placement by this\nsection.\n3.\nDivision 26 - Wiring Connections: Execution requirements for pumps specified\nby this section.\n\n1.02\n\nREFERENCES\n\nA.\n\nFM Global:\n1.\nFM - Approval Guide, A Guide to Equipment, Materials & Services Approved\nBy Factory Mutual Research For Property Conservation.\n\nB.\n\nNational Electrical Manufacturers Association:\n1.\nNEMA 250 - Enclosures for Electrical Equipment (1000 Volts Maximum).\n2.\nNEMA MG 1 - Motors and Generators.\n\nC.\n\nNational Fire Protection Association:\n1.\nNFPA 13 - Installation of Sprinkler Systems.\n2.\nNFPA 14 – Installation of Standpipe and Hose Systems.\n3.\nNFPA 20 - Standard for the Installation of Centrifugal Fire Pumps.\n\nD.\n\nUnderwriters Laboratories Inc.:\n1.\nUL 448 - Pumps for Fire Protection Service.\n2.\nUL 778 - Motor Operated Water Pumps.\n3.\nUL 1478 - Fire Pump Relief Valves.\n4.\nUL - Fire Protection Equipment Directory.\n\n1.03\n\nDESIGN REQUIREMENTS\n\nA.\n\nConform to NFPA 20.\n\nB.\n\nFire Pump System: The fire pump system consists of an (horizontal split-case) fire\npump motor, automatic transfer switch, soft starting fire pump controller, jockey pump,\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fjockey pump motor, jockey pump controller, associated valves, gauges, and test\napparatus to supply water to the combined standpipe & sprinkler system.\n1.\nThe jockey pump maintains a minimum pressure in the combined standpipe &\nsprinkler system.\n2.\nThe fire pump starts in the event of a drop in pressure below the minimum\npressure maintained by the jockey pump.\nC.\n\n1.04\n\nDesign Parameters\n1.\nSize of selected pump is not to be changed from that shown on the Contract\nDrawings unless shown to be inadequate as per calculations to be provided in the\nsprinkler/standpipe system.\n2.\nSubmittals in this section shall not be made until hydraulic calculations provided\nhave been submitted and reviewed.\n3.\nFire pump and controller shall be delivered “broken down” for transport into the\nfire pump room, and field assembled.\nPERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS\n\nA.\n\nConform to NFPA 20.\n\nB.\n\nSeismic Performance: Fire pumps shall withstand the effects of earthquake motions\ndetermined according to ASCE/SEI 7.\n1.\nThe term \"withstand\" means \"the unit will remain in place without separation of\nany parts from the device when subjected to the seismic forces specified and the\nunit will be fully operational after the seismic event.\"\n\nC.\n\nPump Equipment, Accessory, and Specialty Pressure Rating: 300 psig minimum unless\nhigher pressure rating is indicated.\n\n1.05\n\nSUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal procedures.\n\nB.\n\nShop Drawings: Indicate layout, general assembly, components, dimensions, weights,\nclearances and methods of assembly.\n\nC.\n\nProduct Data: Submit manufacturers literature including general assembly, pump curves\nshowing performance characteristics with pump and system, operating point indicated,\nNPSH curve, controls, wiring diagrams and service connections. All Shop Drawings\nshall also be submitted to Electrical for approval.\n\nD.\n\nRigging: The contractor shall submit a rigging plan for bringing the fire pump and\ncontroller/transfer switch to the fire pump room prior to commencing with such work.\n\nE.\n\nTest Reports:\n1.\nFactory performance test: certified test curve for each pump.\n2.\nField acceptance test: Indicate results of hydrostatic test and field acceptance\ntests.\n3.\nComply with Modified NYC Fire Code Chapter 9 Section BC 901 (901.5)\n(Acceptance Test).\n\nF.\n\nManufacturer's Installation Instructions:\nrequirements, for fire pump system.\n\nSubmit\n\nsupport\n\ndetails,\n\nconnection\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 2\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n\fG.\n\nSeismic Qualification Certificates: For fire pumps, accessories, and components, from\nmanufacturer.\n1.\nBasis for Certification: Indicate whether withstand certification is based on\nactual test of assembled components or on calculation.\n2.\nDimensioned Outline Drawings of Equipment Unit: Identify center of gravity\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138923825}}
{"type":"message","id":"14572535","parentId":"a2d684cc","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:15:23.831Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01VHiFjuSYMZepwMqLKZhKz2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"READ CAREFULLY\n\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor\nNew York, NY 10041\n\nSECTION “A “\nBIDDING OFFICE: CONTRACT SERVICES\nPROJECT TITLE:\n\n1120220: Fire Pump & Standpipe\nReplacement at Bellevue Hospital Center\n370 CCDs\n\nALL BIDS SUBMITTED SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TERMS OF\nTHE NYC H+H (HHC) PROJECT LABOR LAW AGREEMENT\n\nNOTICE: ALL BIDDERS MUST REFER TO THE CONTENTS OF THE\nATTACHED BID PACKAGE FOR BIDDER REQUIREMENTS\n\n\fREAD CAREFULLY\nNEW YORK CITY HEALTH AND HOSPITAL CORPORATION\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\nSECTION A\nBID FORMS\nCONSTRUCTIONS CONTRACTS\nUSE THESE BID FORMS ONLY, NOT THOSE IN THE BOOK\nTO ALL BIDDERS:\nALL BIDS SUBMITTED SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TERMS OF THE NYC H+H (HHC) PROJECT LABOR\nAGREEMENT. EACH CONTRACTOR THAT IS AWARED A CONTRACT SHALL BE REQUIRED TO EXECUTE A LETTER\nOF ASSENT AND SUBMIT IT TO NYC H+H\nYou must submit a completed Bid Proposal (Bid Form A‐1, Page 15) and a completed Bid Bond with your Bid.\nFailure to submit a completed Bid Proposal and a completed Bid Bond with your bid and failure to meet the\nterms of the HHC PROJECT LABOR AGREEMENT shall cause your bid to be declared non‐responsive. Failure to\ncomplete and submit all other items in Section “A” may cause you bid to be declared non‐response. Refer to\nthe enclosed checklist when preparing your bid proposal. Your bid proposal will be checked for responsiveness\nfrom this checklist.\nEVERY SPACE MUST BE COMPLETED. IF ITEMS DO NOT APPLY, INSERT N/A. DO NOT LEAVE BLANK SPACES.\n\nSECTION “A” IS AS FOLLOWS\n CONSTRUCTION BID CHECKLIST – PAGE 1A\n BID FORM A‐1,\nPAGE 1\n BID BREAKDOWN:\nPAGE 1 OF 3\n BID FORM A‐1‐1\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO 220 AND 230\n BID FORM A‐1‐2\nINSURANCE INFORMATION\n BID FORMS A‐2\nPAGES 16‐19 (BID BOND IS REQUIRED FOR ALL BIDS OF $50,000 OR MORE)\n WORK EXPERIENCE\nATTACHMENTS AE‐1 – AE‐4\n VENDEX QUESTIONNAIRES (VENDOR ENTITY AND PRINCIPLE QUESTIONNAIRES) FOR ALL BIDS OF\n$100,000 OR MORE. PLEASE USE LINK (https://passport.cityofnewyork.us)\n\nNOTICE\nALL BIDDERS MUST BE ABLE TO SUBSTANTIATE THAT THEY COMPLETED CONTRACT(S) OF SIMILAR SCOPE\nWITH THE PAST FIVE (5) YEARS.\n\nTECHNICAL QUESTIONS MUST BE SUBMITTED IN WRITING NO LATER THAN (DATE IS PROVIDED)\n\n\fCONSTRUCTION BID CHECKLIST\n1. Bid Form A‐1, Bidders Proposal – (page 15)\nTrades, Licensee Name, License Number, License Expiration Date\nAddenda Number (if applicable)\nTotal Lump Sum Bid Price in numbers and Words\nBidder’s company Name/Phone No./Fax No.\nN.Y.S Certified MBE/WBE\nBidder’s Signature and Date\nBidder’s Corporate Seal (if applicable)\n2. Bid Alternate(s) (if applicable)\n\nFILLED IN\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n\nAll Blanks for Dollar Amounts\nIndicate Whether Amount(s) are Additions or Deductions\n\n( )\n( )\n\nBID FORM A‐1.1\nBID FORM A‐1‐2\n\n( )\n( )\n\n3. Bid form A‐2\n\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO 220 AND 230\nINSURANCE CERTIFICATES\n10% Bid Bond – (page 16)\n\n( )\n\nPrincipal’s Name\nSurety Company’s Name\nDollar Amount in Words and Numbers\nProposed Contract (description) (pages 18 & 19)\nPrincipal Signed, Sealed and Notarized\nSurety Signed, Sealed and Notarized\n4. Bid Breakdown\nBidder’s Name and Date\nLocation of Facility, Project No. and Project Title\nItems No. and Item of Work\nColumns 1‐5\nNo. 6 – Total Bid Price\n\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n\n5. Completed Contracts – (pages AE‐1 – AE‐4\nContractor/Subcontractor\nFacility/Project Name/Address\nOwner/Project Manager/Phone No.\nSurety Company/Agent/ Phone No.\nBonding Amount\nContract Award Amount/Contract No.\nAll Dates\nConstruction Manager/Architect/Address/Reference/Phone No.\n\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n\n6. Vendex\n\n( )\n\n( )\n\n\fOffice of Facilities Development, Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442-3680 | Fax: (212) 442-3741\nBID PROPOSAL FOR CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS\nTRADE:\n\nPROJECT ID:\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION:\nALL BIDS USBMITTED SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TERMS OF THE NYC HEALTH + HOSPITAL (HHC) PROJECT LABOR\nAGREEMENT. EACH CONTRACTOR AWARDED A CONTRACT SHALL BE REQUIRED TO EXECUTE A LETTER OF ASSENT AND SUBMIT\nIT TO NYC H+H.\n*LICENSEE: ______________________ LINCENSE NO. __________________ EXPIRATION DATE: ____________\nThe bidder confirms that its bid for the above project includes all work in accordance with the Contract Documents and Addenda.\nAll Addenda must contain the signature of the principal or authorized representative, and the date, and must be submitted with\nthe bid proposal as part of Section “A”. The bidder is to list all said addenda by number as follows:\nAddenda: ____________________ (LIST AND INCLUDE ALL ADDENDA IN BID PACKAGE)\nBASE BID PRICE: _________________________________________________________________________\n(In Words)\nTOTAL BID PRICE: _________________________________________________________________________\n(In Words)\n1. BASE BID PRICE\n$\n2. ALTERNATE # 1 PRICE\n$\n3. ALTERNATE # 2 PRICE\n$\n4. ALTERNATE # 3 PRICE\n$\n5. ALTERNATE # 4 PRICE\n$\n6. ALTERNATE # 5 PRICE\n$\n7. ALTERNATE # 6 PRICE\n$\n8. TOTAL BID PRICE\n$\nBID SECURITY: Bid Security Must Be in the Form of a Bid Bond Only and must be enclosed in the same envelope as the bid.\nBID BOND COMPANY:\n(BID BOND 10% OF BID)\nBIDDER:\n(FULL COMPANY NAME)\nPHONE/FAX/E-MAIL:\n\nN.Y.S. CERTIFIED MBE/WBE:\n(PLEASE PRINT WHICH ONE, IF NONE PLEASE PRINT N/A)\nEIN/SSN No.:\nBY:\n(PRINT NAME OF OWNER OR CORPORATE OFFICER)\n(SIGNATURE OF OWNER OR CORPORATE OFFICER)\nDATE:\nATTEST:\nNOTE:\n\n(EVERY SPACE MUST BE COMPLETED CORPORATE SEAL)\n(IF IT DOES NOT APPPLY, PLEASE INSERT N/A)\n\nIn case of any discrepancy between the price in words and that in figures the Lower Price Shall be considered the bid\nprice.\n*NAME OF THE PERSON OR FIRM THAT APPEARS ON THE LICENSE.\nALL BIDDERS: PLEASE USE THE FORM THAT IS PROVIEDED WITH THE PROJECT’S BID PACKAGE.\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\nBID FORM A-1\n\n\fEXHIBIT “A”\nARTICLE 15A\nMANDATORY NEW YORK STATE CERTIFIED\nMINORITY & WOMEN BUSINESS ENTERPRISES GOALS FOR SUBCONTRACTORS & SUPPLIES\n\nPROJECT NAME:\n\n11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump & Standpipe Replacement\n\nCONTRACT GOALS\nTOTAL % M/WBE GOAL\n30%\n\nContract # 1\n\nForm B‐1 “Bidder M/WBE Utilization Plan “in section “B” submitted by the lowest bidder will be compared to\nthe goals set forth above.\n\n14 A\n\n\fInsert bid breakdown pages\n\n\fOffice of Facilities Development/ Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442‐3680 Fax: (212) 442‐3741\n\nALTERNATES NO. 1 ‐ 6\n11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump &\nStandpipe Replacement\n\nNOTE:\n\nIMPORTANT\n\nThis solicitation contains Alternates 1‐6. The Corporation shall reserve the right select the Base Bid and /or\nAlternate No. 1 and / or Alternate No. 2. and/or Alternate No. 3., and/or Alternate No. , and/or Alternate No.\n5, and/or Alternate No. 6. In the event that the Corporation elects to award Alternate No. 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 or any\ncombination of Alternates No. 1-6, the responsive bidder submitting the lowest aggregate bid price (Base Bid\n+ Alternates Selected at the NYC HHC's Discretion) shall be determined to be the apparent lowest bidder for\nthis solicitation. The responsive bidder submitting the lowest base bid shall be determined to be the apparent\nlow bidder for this solicitation.\n\n\fOffice of Facilities Development/ Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442‐3680 Fax: (212) 442‐3741\n\nATTACHMET NO. 1 TO BID PROPOSAL\nALL CONTRACTS\nNOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO. 220 &\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO. 230\nAll contractors awarded contracts by New York City Health + Hospitals and all subcontractors working for those\ncontractors on New York City Health + Hospitals projects shall be required to notify each of their employees on\nsuch projects of the applicable prevailing wage for his or her job classification. This notification shall appear on\neach employee’s pay stub. In addition, the first paycheck given to employees at the project site, and the first\npaycheck given to employees at the project site after each successive July 1, shall be accompanied by a notice\nidentifying the public body. Such notice shall also inform employees of their right to contact the designated\npublic body if prevailing wages are not paid. Contact should be made through the Construction Management\nOffice of the New York City Health + Hospitals’ Facility where the work is being performed.\n\nAgreed:\nName of Contractor:\nBy: (Officer or Authorized) Representative: ________________________\nPrint\n__________________________________\nSignature\n\n__________________________\nDate\n\nTitle: ___________________________________________\nPrint\n\nBID FORM A‐1.1\n\n\fOffice of Facilities Development/ Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442‐3680 Fax: (212) 442‐3741\n\nName of Contractor: ___________________________\n\nProject Name: __________________________\n\nATTACHEMENT:\n\nNO. 2 TO BID PROPOSAL ‐ ALL CONTRACTS\n\nIMPROTANT:\n\nAll Insurance Carriers that will be providing coverage for New York Health + Hospitals\ncontacts shall be licensed and authorized/ admitted to be business in New York State.\n\nALL BIDDERS ARE REQUIRED TO COMPLETE THIS FORM AND SUBMIT IT WITH THEIR BID\n\nType of Coverage\n\nName of Insurance Carrier\n\nNAIC No.\n\nCommercial General Liability\nAutomobile Liability\nExcess/Umbrella\nWorker’s Compensation\nDisability Benefits\nAll Risk/Builders Risk\nIt is requested that an original Insurance Certificate substantiating the insurance coverage described above, be\nsubmitted to NYC H + H when the lowest responsive and responsible bidder returns its executed contract.\n\nSigned By: ________________________________________\n\nDate: ______________________________\n\nPrint Name: ________________________________________\nTitle: ______________________________________________\n\nBID FORM A‐1.2 Rev. 1/8/16\n\n\fFORM OF BID BOND\nKNOW ALL MEN BY THESE PRESENTS, that we__________________________________\n___________________________________________________________________________________\nhereinafter referred to as the “Principal,” and_______________________________________________\n__________________________________________________________________________________\nHereinafter referred to as the “Surety” are held and firmly bound to the New York City Health and Hospitals\nCorporation hereinafter referred to as the “Corporation” or to its successors and assigns, in the penal sum\nof_________________________________________________________________________________\n($______________________) Dollars, lawful money of the United States for the payment of which said sum of money will\nand truly to be made, we, and each of us, bind ourselves, our heirs, executors, administrators, successors, and assigns,\njointly and severally, firmly by these presents.\nWHEREAS, the Principal is about to submit (or has submitted) to the Corporation the accompanying proposal,\nhereby made a part hereof, to enter into a contract in writing\nfor________________________________________________________________________________________________\n__________________________________________________________________________________________________\nNOW, THEREFORE, the conditions of this obligation are such that the Principal shall not withdraw any Proposals\nwithout the consent of the Corporation for a period of forty‐five (45) days after the opening of bids, one hundred\nand twenty (120) days after the opening of bids where the project has one or more contracts with a bid of one\nmillion dollars ($1,000,000) or more and, in event of acceptance of the Principal’s Proposals by the Corporation if\nthe Principal shall:\nA.\n\nwithin five (5) days after notification by the Corporation execute and deliver six (6) copies to the\nCorporation of all the executed counterparts of the Contract in the form set forth in the Contract\nDocuments, in accordance with proposal as accepted;\n\nB.\n\nfurnish a Performance Bond and separate Payment Bond, as may be required by the Corporation for the\nfaithful performance and proper fulfillment of such Contract, which bonds shall be satisfactory in all\nrespects to the Corporation, shall be executed by good and sufficient sureties; and;\n\nC.\n\nin all respects performs the agreement created by the acceptance of said Proposal as provided in the\ninformation for Bidders, bound herewith and hereby made a part hereof, or if the Corporation shall reject\nthe aforesaid Proposal, then this obligation shall be null and void; otherwise to remain in full force and\neffect.\n\nIn the event that the Proposal of the Principal shall be accepted and the Contract be awarded to him, the Surety\nhereunder agrees, subject only to the payment by the Principal of the premium therefore, if requested by the\nCorporation to write the aforementioned Performance and Payment bonds in the form set forth in the Contract\nDocuments.\nIt is expressly understood and agreed that the liability of the Surety for any and all claims hereunder shall in no\nevent exceed the penal amount of this obligation as herein stated.\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\n\nBID FORM A‐2\n‐16‐\n\n\fThere shall be no liability under this bond if, in the event of acceptance of the Principals Proposal by the Corporation,\neither a Performance Bond or Payment Bond or both, shall not be required by the Corporation on or before the 30th day\nafter the date on which the Corporation signs the Contract.\nThe Surety, for value received, hereby stipulates and agrees that the obligations of the Surety and its bond shall\nin no way be impaired or affected by any postponements of the day upon which the Corporation will receive or\nopen bids, or by any extensions of the time within which the Corporation may accept the Principal’s Proposal or\nby any waiver by the Corporation of the requirements of the Information for Bidders; and the Surety hereby\nwaives notice of any such postponements, extensions or waivers.\n\nSURETY COMPANY MUST BE LICENSED TO DO BUSINESS IN THE STATE OF NEW YORK\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\n\nBID FORM A‐2\n\n‐17‐\n\n\fIN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Principal and the Surety have hereunto set their hands and seeks and such of them\nas are a Corporation have caused their corporate seals to be hereto affixed and these presents to be signed by\ntheir proper officers the ______________________ day of _______________in the year__________.\nBY _________________________________ (L.S.)\n(Principal Signature)\n\n(Seal)\n\nBY__________________________________\n(Surety Signature)\n\n(Seal)\n\nBY _________________________________\n*****************\nACKNOWLEDGMENT OF PRINCIPAL, IF A CORPORATION\n\nSTATE OF :___________________________)\nSS:\nCOUNTY OF _________________________)\nOn this _____________________ day of ______________in the year____________ before me\npersonally came_____________________________ to me known, who being by me duly sworn\ndid depose and say that he resides at_________________________________________________\n_______________________________________________________________________________\nthat he is the __________________________ of________________________________________\n_______________________________________________________________________________\nthe corporation described in and which executed the foregoing instrument; that he knows the seal of said\ncorporation; that one of the seals affixed to said instrument is such seal; that it was affixed by one of the\ndirectors of said corporation, and that he signed his name there by like order.\n\n______________________________________\n(