D,\nare requested to complete the questions asked below and return this form, in the envelope provided, in time for\nbid opening.\n********************************************************************************************\n*********\nNAME OF PROJECT:\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement\n\nFACILITY/CAMPUS:\n\nBellevue Hospital Center\n\nREASON(S) FOR NOT BIDDING AT THIS TIME:\n\nVENDOR’S NAME: ___________________________________________________________________________\nVENDOR’S ADDRESS: _________________________________________________________________________\n\n______________________________________\nSIGNATURE\n\n_________________________________________\nTITLE\n\nIT IS NOT NECESSARY FOR VENDORS WHO ARE SUBMITTING BIDS ON THE SUBJECT SPECIFIED HEREIN TO RETURN\nTHIS FORM.\n\n\fREAD CAREFULLY\nNEW YORK CITY HEALTH AND HOSPITALS CORPORATION\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\nSECTION “B” FOR CONSTRUCTION\nBID FORMS\nUSE THESE BID FORMS ONLY, NOT THOSE IN THE BOOK\nTO ALL BIDDERS:\nTHE LOWEST RESPONSIVE BIDDERS MUST COMPLETE AND SUBMIT ALL FORMS IN SECTION “B” AS SHOWN\nBELOW BY THE CLOSE OF THE SECOND BUSINESS DAY AFTER THE BID OPENING OR THEIR BID PROPOSAL\nMAY BE DEEMED NOT RESPONSIBLE. IT IS THE BIDDERS RESPONSIBILITY TO ASCERTAIN IF THEY ARE THE\nLOWEST BIDDER.\n\nSECTION “B” FORMS FOR ALL BIDS\nBID FORM B-1\nBID FORM B-1A\nBID FORM B-2\nBID FORM B-3\nBID FORM B-4\nBID FORM B-5\nBID FORMS B-6\nBID FORM B-6A\n\nWORK TO BE SUBCONTRACTED\nMBE AND WBE UTILIZATION PLAN\nACKNOWLEDGMENT OF BIDDER\nNON-COLLUSION AND TAX AFFIRMATION\nAPPRENTICESHIP PROGRAM, HEALTH AND\nWELFARE AND PENSION PROGRAM\nDOING BUSINESS IN NORTHERN IRELAND\nBIDDERS CORPORATE RESOLUTION AND\nAFFIDAVIT\nAGREEMENT\n\nPAGE 20\nPAGE 20A-B (2 pages)\nPAGE 21\nPAGES 22-24\nPAGE 25\nPAGE 26\nPAGES 27-32\nPAGES 33\n\nCOMPLETE ALL OF THE ABOVE FORMS, SIGNED AND DATED AS INDICATED.\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\n\n\fWORK TO BE SUBCONTRACTED\nDO YOU ANTICIPATE SUBCONTRACTING ANY PORTION OF THE WORK ON THIS PROJECT?\nYES\n\nNO\n\nIf yes, please list below all scopes of work to be sub-contracted and indicate: 1. If MWBE to perform scope Y/N;\n2. Name of vendor to perform work; and 3. Approximate dollar value of work to be performed:\n\nMWBE\n(Y/N)\n\nScope of Work\n\nApproximate Cost\n($)\n\nVendor\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n\nTotal Amount (Must equal total bid amount):\n\nContractor’s Signature\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\n\n$\n\nDate\nBid Form B-1\n20\n\n\fSAVE\n\nCLEAR\n\nHHC-100HHC\nREV. 11/2021\n\nM/WBE Utilization Plan\nInstructions - In the area below, please provide the business full legal name, such as \"ABC Company, Inc.\" or \"ABC Firm, LLC\". Please also provide the contact\ninformation of the person responsible for the compliance and reporting functions under this agreement.\nSolicitation Name\n\nSolicitation M/WBE Goal\n\nVendor Full Legal Name\n\nVendor Tax ID#\n\nAddress\n\nTelephone #\n\nVendor M/WBE Compliance Contact Name\n\nEmail\n\n%\n\nInstructions - In the table below, briefly describe the scope of work for each M/WBE subcontractor, such as \"Electrical work\", \"Training\", \"Furniture\". List the percentage\nof the scope of work against the total estimated value of the contract. For example, if this is a three year contract worth $100 a year, and the subcontractor's work is a\ntotal of $90 over the three years, the percent would be equal to $90/($100 * 3 years) or 30%. Note M/WBE vendors must be certified by New York State or New York\nCity to qualify. If additional space is needed please use table provided on page 2.\nNYS/NYC Certified M/WBE Subcontractors/Suppliers\nPlease ensure combined M/WBE Goal calculated below meets or exceeds the solicitation M/WBE goal. If through good faith efforts, the solicitation M/WBE Goal\ncannot be met, please complete the Waiver Request Form. \t\t\nNYS/NYC Certified M/WBE\nSubcontractors/Suppliers\nFull Legal Name\n\nSub\nPoint Of Contact\n\nSub\nEmail\n\nSub\nTelephone\n\nSub\nTax ID\n\n% of\n\nCertification\nType\n\nScopes of Work\n\nSubcontracts/\n\nsupplies/\nservices\n\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\nCombined M/WBE utilization goal (sum of percentages)\n\n0 %\n\nSubmission of this form constitutes the vendor’s acknowledgement and agreement to comply with the M/WBE requirements set forth as part of the solicitation. Failure to provide complete and\naccurate information may result in a rejection of the bid/proposal, and noncompliance with the goals may result in termination of the resulting contract, monetary damages, and debarment.\n\nPrepared By (Signature)\nName (Print)\n\nTelephone no.\n\nTitle of Preparer (Print)\n\nEmail address\n1 of 2\n\n\fHHC-100HHC\nREV. 11/2021\n\nAdditional NYS/NYC Certified M/WBE Subcontractors/Suppliers\n\nNYS/NYC Certified M/WBE\nSubcontractors/Suppliers\nFull Legal Name\n\nSub\nPoint Of Contact\n\nSub\nEmail\n\nSub\nTelephone\n\nSub\nTax ID\n\nCertification\nType\n\n% of\n\nScopes of Work\n\nSubcontracts/\n\nsupplies/\nservices\n\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n\n2 of 2\n\n\fACKNOWLEDGMENT\nName of Bidder:\nBidder is Individual ( ) Partnership ( ) Corporation ( ) Joint Venture\n{Check one, as case may be}\n\nPlace of Business of Bidder:\n\nResidence of Bidder (*If Individual):\n\nTelephone No:\nDate of Bid:\n\n******************************\n\nIf the Bidder is a Partnership, or Joint Venture, fill in the following blanks\nName of Partners\n\nResidence of Partner\n\nBID FORM B-2\n\n21\n\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\n\fNON COLLUSION AND TAX AFFIRMATION\n********************\n\nIf the Bidder is a Corporation, fill in the following blanks\nOrganized Under the laws of the State of:\n\nName and Home Address of President:\n\nName and Home Address of Secretary:\n\nName and Home Address of Treasures:\n\n********************************\nThe above-named bidder affirms and declares:\n1. The said bidder is of a lawful age and the only person interested in the bid: and that no, firm or\ncorporation other than herein above-named has any interest in this bid, or in the Contracts proposed to be\ntaken.\n2. BIDDER’S CERTIFICATE RE: NON-COLLUSION - By submission of the bid, each bidder and each person\nsigning on behalf of any bidder certified, and in the case of joint bid each party thereto certifies as to its\nown organization, under penalty of perjury, that to their best knowledge and behalf:\nA. The prices in this bid have been arrived at independently without, collusion, consultation,\ncommunication, or agreement for the purpose of restricting competition, as to any matter relating\nto such prices with any other bidder or with any competitor.\nB. Unless otherwise required by law, the prices which have been quoted in this bid have not been\nknowingly disclosed by the bidder prior to opening, directly or indirectly to any other bidder or to\nany competitor: and\nC. No attempt has been made or will be made by the Bidder to induce any other person, partnership,\nor corporation to submit or not to submit a bid for the purpose of restricting competition.\n\n22\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\n\f3. That no councilman or other officer or employee or person whose salary is payable in whole or impart\nfrom the City Treasury is directly or indirectly interested in this bid, or in the supplies, materials,\nequipment, work or labor to which it is related, or in any of the profits thereof.\n4. The said bidder is not in arrears to the City of New York upon any debt or contractor taxes and is a\ndefaulter, as surety or otherwise, upon any obligation to the City of New York, and has not been declared\nnot responsible or disqualified, by any agency of the City of New York or the State of New York, nor is\nthere any proceeding pending relating to the responsibly or qualification of the Bidder to receive public\ncontract\n(If none, the bidder will insert “NONE.”)\n5. The undersigned, if an individual bidder, or if the bidder be a firm, partnership or corporation, the\nundersigned executing this document, as a member, partner, director or officer and on behalf of such\nfirm, partnership, or corporation, expressly warrants and represents that neither he, nor any member,\npartner, director or officer of said firms, partnership or corporation has, prior to the date of execution\nof this bid, bee called before a grand jury, head of state department, temporary state commission or\nother state agency, to testify in an investigation concerning any transaction or contract he has with the\nState of New York, any political subdivision thereof, a public authority, or with any public department,\nagency or official of the state of New York or of any subdivision against subsequent criminal prosecution\nor to answer any relevant question concerning such transaction or contract.\nIf there has been a refusal to sign a waiver or to answer, the bidder must state the time and place of\nsuch refusal in the following spaces:\nDate:\n\nPlace:\n\nName of Bidder:\n6. The bidder, as an individual, or as a member, partner, director or officer of the bidder, if the same be a\nfirm, partnership or corporation, executes this document expressly warranting and representing that\nshould this bid be accepted by the Corporation and the Contract awarded him, he and is subcontractors\nengaged in the performance of the Contract: (1) will comply with the provisions of Section 343-8.0 of\nthe Administrative Code of the City of New York and the non-discrimination provisions of Section 3439.0 of the Administrative code of the City of New York in relation to minimum wages and other\nstipulations and the rules and regulations of the Board of Estimate adopted pursuant thereto as more\nexpressively and in detail set forth in the Contract form; (2) have compiled with aforesaid laws and rules\nand regulations since their respective effective dates insofar as applicable to the bidder and to his\nsubcontractor; and (3) will post notice, to be furnished by the Corporation, setting forth the\nrequirements of the aforesaid laws in prominent and conspicuous place in each and every plant, factory,\nbuilding and structure where employee engaged in the performance of the Contract con readily view it,\nand will continue to keep such notices posted until the supplies, materials, and equipment or work, labor\nand services required to be finished or rendered by the Contractor have been finally accepted by the\nCorporation.\n\n23\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\n\fIf there has been a breach or violation of the aforesaid Section 343-9.0 or of the aforesaid rules and\nregulations, the Bidder must state the time, place and circumstances of such breach or violation of the\nbid form submitted.\nIn event of breach or violation of any of the foregoing, the Bidder may be subject to damaged, liquidated\nor otherwise, cancellation of the Contract and suspension as a bidder for a period of three years.\n(The words, “the bidder”, “he”, his”, where used herein shall mean the individual bidder, firm\npartnership, or corporation executing his bid form).\nThe bidder, as an individual, or member, partner director, or officer of the bidder, if the same be a firm,\npartnership, or corporation: (1) represents that his attention has been specifically drawn to Article 34A\nEqual Employment Compliance of the Contract Agreement: and (2) warrants that he will comply with\nthe provisions of this article.\nThe bidder as an individual, or as a member, partner, director or officer of the Bidder, if the same be a\nfirm, partnership, or corporation, executes this documents expressly warranting that he will comply with\nthe provisions of the Contract Agreement on providing records, Section4. (6) of Article 36A on equal\nEmployment Compliance.\n7. That said bidder has visited and examined the site of the work and has carefully examined the Contract\nin the form approved by the General Counsel, and will execute the Contract and perform all its terms\ncovenants and conditions, and will provide, furnish and deliver all the work, materials, supplies, tools,\nand appliance for all labor and materials necessary or required for the herein before named work, all in\nstrict conformity with the Contract.\n8. The said bidder affirms that it has paid all applicable City income, excise and other taxes for all years it\nhas conducted business activities in New York\n\nDate:\n\nTax Identification No.\n\nName of Bidder:\nBy:\n\n24\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\n\fAPPRENTICESHIP PROGRAM HEALTH AND WELFARE AND PENSION PLAN\n(Complete this form if your bid is over (250,000.00)\n(See Section No. 18 Information for Bidders)\n1.\n\na.\n\nHave you utilized apprentices on N.Y.C contracts in the past?\n\nb.\nDo you and/ or your subcontractors intend to utilize the services of apprentices on this\ncontract?\nIf NO to part (b) you will be precluded from doing so in this project. If YES specify the New York\nState indentured apprenticeship program, under which apprentices were employed and will be\nemployed:\n\n2.\n\nDo you have a participating health and welfare program for your employees?\nIf YES, give name of carrier and employer identification number:\n\n3.\n\nDo you have a pension plan providing coverage for your employees?\nIf YES give the name of carrier and employer identification number:\n\nBidder:\nBy:\nSignature of Partner or Corporate Officer\n\n25\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\n\fCERTIFICATION REGARDING BUSINESS DEALINGS WITH NORTHERN IRELAND\nA.\n\nThe Contractor and any individual or legal entity in which the Contractor holds ten percent or greater ownership\ninterest and any individual or legal entity that holds a ten percent or greater ownership or interests in the\nContractor either (a) has no business operations in Northern Ireland, or (b) shall take lawful steps in good faith to\nconduct any business operations with Northern Ireland in accordance with the MacBride Principles, and shall\npermit independent monitoring of their compliance with such principles.\n\nB.\n\nFor the purposes of this Certification, “MacBride Principles” shall mean those principles relating to\nnondiscrimination in employment and freedom of workplace opportunity which requires employers doing business\nin Northern Ireland to:\n1. increase the representation of individuals from under represented religious groups in the work force,\nincluding managerial, supervisory, administrative, clerical, and technical jobs;\n2. take steps to promote adequate security for the protection of employees from under represented religious\ngroups, both at the workplace and while traveling to and from work;\n3. ban provocative religious or political emblems from the workplace;\n4. publicly advertise all job openings and make special recruitment efforts to attract applicants from under\nrepresented religious groups;\n5. establish layoff, recall and termination procedures which do not in practice favor a particular religious group;\n6. abolish all job reservations, apprenticeship restrictions and different employment criteria which\ndiscriminates on the basis of religion;\n7. Develop training programs that will prepare substantial numbers of current employees from under\nrepresented religious groups for skilled jobs, including the expansion of existing programs and the creation\nof new programs to train, upgrade and improve the skills of workers from under-represented religious\ngroups;\n8. establish procedures to assess, identify and actively recruit employees from under represented religious groups\nwith potential for further advancement ; and\n9. appoint a senior management staff member to oversee affirmative action efforts to develop a timetable to\nensure their full implementation.\n\nC.\n\nThe Contractor agrees that the warranties and representations in paragraph A are material conditions of this\nAgreement. If the Corporation receives information that the Contractor is in violation of paragraph A, the\nCorporation shall review such information and give the relevant party opportunity to respond. If the\nCorporation finds that a violation has occurred, the Corporation may declare the Contractor in default, and/or\nterminate this Agreement. In the event of any such termination, thee Corporation may procure the supplies,\nservices or work from another source in any manner the Corporation deems proper. The Contractor shall pay\nto the Corporation, or the Corporation, in its sole discretion, may withhold any amounts otherwise payablele\nto the Contractor, the difference between the contract price for the uncompleted portion of this Agreement\nand the cost to the Corporation of completing performance of this agreement either by itself or by engaging\nanother contractor. If this is a requirements contract, the Contractor shall be liable for the difference in price\nfor the entire amount of supplies required by the Corporation for the uncompleted term of this Agreement. If\nthis is a construction contract, the Corporation shall also have the right to hold the Contractor in partial or total\ndefault in accordance with the default provisions of this Agreement. In addition, the e Contractor may be\ndeclared a non- responsible bidder or proposer for up to three years, following written notice to the\nContractor, giving the Contractor the opportunity for a hearing at which the Contractor may be represented\nby counsel. The rights and remedies of the Corporation hereunder shall be in addition to, and not in lieu of,\nany rights and remedies the Corporation haspursuant to this Agreement or by operation of law or equity.\n\nAgreed:\nName of Contractor:\nBy: (Authorized Representative)\nTitle:\n\nDate:\n26\n\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\n\fBIDDERS CORPORATE RESOLUTION AND AFFIDAVIT\nResolved that\n\n(Name of Corporation)\n\nBe authorized to sign and submit the bid or proposal of this corporation for the project described on the Bid\nForm an to include in such bid or proposal the Certificate as to Non-Collusion required by section one hundred\nthree-d (103-d) of the general municipal law as the act and deed of such corporation, and for any inaccuracies\nor misstatements in such certificate this corporate bidder shall be liable under penalties of perjury.\nThe foregoing is a true and correct copy of the resolution adopted by:\n\nCorporation at a meeting of its Board of Director held on this\n\nday of\n\nin the year\n\n.\n\n(SEAL OF CORPORATION)\nSecretary\nAffidavit on Page 31 should be subscribed and sworn to before a Notary Public or Commissioner of Deeds.\n*Note:\n\nIn case of any discrepancy between the price on words and that is figures, the LOWEST PRICE will be\nconsidered the price bid.\nEXPEMPTION FROM NEW YORK STATE AND LOCAL SALES AND USED TAX\n\nFor the purpose of complying with and obtaining the exemption provided by Section 1115 (a) (15) of the new\nYork State Tax Law, as added by Laws of 1969, Chapter 479, for New York State Tax and Compensating Use Tax\nfor the purchase or maternal required by this contract, except materials consumed by the contractor in the\nperformant thereof. The contractor, when bidding, should not include an amount to cover such New York\nState or New York City taxes.\nA. The Corporation (City) is exempt form payment of Federal, State and local taxes and Sales Compensating\nUse Tax of the State of New York and of cities and countries on all materials and supplies sold to the\nCorporation pursuant to the provisions of this contract.\n27\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\n\fThese taxes are not included in bids. However, this exemption does not apply to tools, machinery,\nequipment, or other property leased by the Contractor or a subcontractor, or to supplies and materials\nwhich, even though they are consumed, are not incorporated in the work (consumable supplies and the\nContractor and his subcontractor shall be responsible for and pay any and all applicable taxes, including\nSales and Compensating Use Taxes, on such leased tools, machinery, equipment, or other property and\nupon all such incorporated supplies and materials.\nB. The contractor agrees to sell and the Corporation agrees to purchase all supplies and materials, other than\nconsumable supplies, required necessary, proper or incidental to the construction of the Project covered\nby this Agreement. The sum paid under this Agreement for such supplies and material shall be in full\npayment for consideration for the sale of such supplies and material under this agreement.\nThe Contractor agrees to construct the Project and to perform all work, labor and services required,\nnecessary or proper for or incidental thereto for the sum shown in the Bid or for sum so paid pursuant to\nthis Agreement for such work, labor, et, shall be in full consideration for the performance by the Contractor\nof all his duties an obligations under this Agreement.\nC. The purchase by the Contractor of the supplies and material sold hereunder shall be a purchase of resale\nand therefore not subject to the New York State or New York City Sales or Compensation Use Taxes or any\nsuch taxes of Cities or counties. The sale of such supplies and materials by the Contractor to the\nCorporation is exempt from the aforesaid sales or compensating use taxes. The Contractor, with respect\nto such supplies and material, at the request of the Corporation, shall furnish to the Corporation such bills\nof sale and other instruments as may be required by it, properly executed, acknowledged and delivered\nassuring to the Corporation title, and the Contractor shall mark or otherwise identify all such materials as\nthe property of the Corporation.\nD. Title of all materials to be sold by the Contractor to the Corporation pursuant to the prevision of the\ncontract shall immediately vest in and become the sole property of the Corporation upon delivery of such\nsupplies and materials to the site and prior to its becoming a part of the permanent structure.\nNotwithstanding such transfer of tile, the Contractor shall have full and continuing responsibility to install\nsuch materials and supplies in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement, to protect them, maintain\nthem in proper condition and forthwith repair, replace and make good any damage thereto, theft or\ndisappearance thereof and furnish additional materials in place to the Corporation until such time as the\nwork covered by the Contract is fully accepted by the Corporation. Such transfer of title shall in no way\naffect any of the Contractor’s obligation hereunder. In the event that after title has passed to the\nCorporation any of such supplies and materials are rejected as being defective or otherwise unsatisfactory\ntitle to all such supplies and material shall be deemed to have been transferred back to the contractor.\n\n28\n\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\n\fE. The purchase by subcontractor supplies and materials to be sold hereunder shall also be a purchase or\nprocurement for resale to the Contractor (either directly or through other subcontracts) and therefore not\nsubject to the aforesaid Sales or compensating Use Taxes, provided that the subcontract agreements\nprovide for the resale of such supplies and materials prior to and separate and apart from the incorporation\nof such supplies and materials into the permanent construction, that such agreements are in from similar\nto this contract with respect to the separation of the sale of materials, from the work and labor, services,\nconsumable supplies and any other matters to be provided, and provided further that the subcontract\nagreement provide separate prices for (1) materials. Such separation shall actually be followed in practice,\nincluding the separation of payments for supplies and materials from payments for other work and labor\nand other things to be provided.\nF. The Contractor and his subcontractors and materialmen shall obtain any and all necessary Contractor\nExempt Purchase Certificate or resale certificates from the appropriate governmental agency or agencies,\nand furnish a Contractor Exempt Purchase Certificate or resale certificate to al person, firms or corporations\nfrom which they purchase supplies and materials for the performance of the work covered by this contract.\nG. In the event any of the provisions of the agreement to which this is an addendum shall be deemed to be in\nconflict with this addendum or shall create any ambiguity, then the addendum shall control.\n\n********************\n\n29\n\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\n\fAffidavit Where Bidder is an Individual\n\nSTAE OF NEW YORK, COUNTY OF:\n\nSS:\n\n[Showing lines 1-1370 of 1509 (50.0KB limit). Use offset=1371 to continue.]"}],"details":{"truncation":{"content":"READ CAREFULLY\n\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor\nNew York, NY 10041\n\nSECTION “A “\nBIDDING OFFICE: CONTRACT SERVICES\nPROJECT TITLE:\n\n1120220: Fire Pump & Standpipe\nReplacement at Bellevue Hospital Center\n370 CCDs\n\nALL BIDS SUBMITTED SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TERMS OF\nTHE NYC H+H (HHC) PROJECT LABOR LAW AGREEMENT\n\nNOTICE: ALL BIDDERS MUST REFER TO THE CONTENTS OF THE\nATTACHED BID PACKAGE FOR BIDDER REQUIREMENTS\n\n\fREAD CAREFULLY\nNEW YORK CITY HEALTH AND HOSPITAL CORPORATION\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\nSECTION A\nBID FORMS\nCONSTRUCTIONS CONTRACTS\nUSE THESE BID FORMS ONLY, NOT THOSE IN THE BOOK\nTO ALL BIDDERS:\nALL BIDS SUBMITTED SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TERMS OF THE NYC H+H (HHC) PROJECT LABOR\nAGREEMENT. EACH CONTRACTOR THAT IS AWARED A CONTRACT SHALL BE REQUIRED TO EXECUTE A LETTER\nOF ASSENT AND SUBMIT IT TO NYC H+H\nYou must submit a completed Bid Proposal (Bid Form A‐1, Page 15) and a completed Bid Bond with your Bid.\nFailure to submit a completed Bid Proposal and a completed Bid Bond with your bid and failure to meet the\nterms of the HHC PROJECT LABOR AGREEMENT shall cause your bid to be declared non‐responsive. Failure to\ncomplete and submit all other items in Section “A” may cause you bid to be declared non‐response. Refer to\nthe enclosed checklist when preparing your bid proposal. Your bid proposal will be checked for responsiveness\nfrom this checklist.\nEVERY SPACE MUST BE COMPLETED. IF ITEMS DO NOT APPLY, INSERT N/A. DO NOT LEAVE BLANK SPACES.\n\nSECTION “A” IS AS FOLLOWS\n CONSTRUCTION BID CHECKLIST – PAGE 1A\n BID FORM A‐1,\nPAGE 1\n BID BREAKDOWN:\nPAGE 1 OF 3\n BID FORM A‐1‐1\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO 220 AND 230\n BID FORM A‐1‐2\nINSURANCE INFORMATION\n BID FORMS A‐2\nPAGES 16‐19 (BID BOND IS REQUIRED FOR ALL BIDS OF $50,000 OR MORE)\n WORK EXPERIENCE\nATTACHMENTS AE‐1 – AE‐4\n VENDEX QUESTIONNAIRES (VENDOR ENTITY AND PRINCIPLE QUESTIONNAIRES) FOR ALL BIDS OF\n$100,000 OR MORE. PLEASE USE LINK (https://passport.cityofnewyork.us)\n\nNOTICE\nALL BIDDERS MUST BE ABLE TO SUBSTANTIATE THAT THEY COMPLETED CONTRACT(S) OF SIMILAR SCOPE\nWITH THE PAST FIVE (5) YEARS.\n\nTECHNICAL QUESTIONS MUST BE SUBMITTED IN WRITING NO LATER THAN (DATE IS PROVIDED)\n\n\fCONSTRUCTION BID CHECKLIST\n1. Bid Form A‐1, Bidders Proposal – (page 15)\nTrades, Licensee Name, License Number, License Expiration Date\nAddenda Number (if applicable)\nTotal Lump Sum Bid Price in numbers and Words\nBidder’s company Name/Phone No./Fax No.\nN.Y.S Certified MBE/WBE\nBidder’s Signature and Date\nBidder’s Corporate Seal (if applicable)\n2. Bid Alternate(s) (if applicable)\n\nFILLED IN\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n\nAll Blanks for Dollar Amounts\nIndicate Whether Amount(s) are Additions or Deductions\n\n( )\n( )\n\nBID FORM A‐1.1\nBID FORM A‐1‐2\n\n( )\n( )\n\n3. Bid form A‐2\n\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO 220 AND 230\nINSURANCE CERTIFICATES\n10% Bid Bond – (page 16)\n\n( )\n\nPrincipal’s Name\nSurety Company’s Name\nDollar Amount in Words and Numbers\nProposed Contract (description) (pages 18 & 19)\nPrincipal Signed, Sealed and Notarized\nSurety Signed, Sealed and Notarized\n4. Bid Breakdown\nBidder’s Name and Date\nLocation of Facility, Project No. and Project Title\nItems No. and Item of Work\nColumns 1‐5\nNo. 6 – Total Bid Price\n\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n\n5. Completed Contracts – (pages AE‐1 – AE‐4\nContractor/Subcontractor\nFacility/Project Name/Address\nOwner/Project Manager/Phone No.\nSurety Company/Agent/ Phone No.\nBonding Amount\nContract Award Amount/Contract No.\nAll Dates\nConstruction Manager/Architect/Address/Reference/Phone No.\n\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n\n6. Vendex\n\n( )\n\n( )\n\n\fOffice of Facilities Development, Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442-3680 | Fax: (212) 442-3741\nBID PROPOSAL FOR CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS\nTRADE:\n\nPROJECT ID:\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION:\nALL BIDS USBMITTED SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TERMS OF THE NYC HEALTH + HOSPITAL (HHC) PROJECT LABOR\nAGREEMENT. EACH CONTRACTOR AWARDED A CONTRACT SHALL BE REQUIRED TO EXECUTE A LETTER OF ASSENT AND SUBMIT\nIT TO NYC H+H.\n*LICENSEE: ______________________ LINCENSE NO. __________________ EXPIRATION DATE: ____________\nThe bidder confirms that its bid for the above project includes all work in accordance with the Contract Documents and Addenda.\nAll Addenda must contain the signature of the principal or authorized representative, and the date, and must be submitted with\nthe bid proposal as part of Section “A”. The bidder is to list all said addenda by number as follows:\nAddenda: ____________________ (LIST AND INCLUDE ALL ADDENDA IN BID PACKAGE)\nBASE BID PRICE: _________________________________________________________________________\n(In Words)\nTOTAL BID PRICE: _________________________________________________________________________\n(In Words)\n1. BASE BID PRICE\n$\n2. ALTERNATE # 1 PRICE\n$\n3. ALTERNATE # 2 PRICE\n$\n4. ALTERNATE # 3 PRICE\n$\n5. ALTERNATE # 4 PRICE\n$\n6. ALTERNATE # 5 PRICE\n$\n7. ALTERNATE # 6 PRICE\n$\n8. TOTAL BID PRICE\n$\nBID SECURITY: Bid Security Must Be in the Form of a Bid Bond Only and must be enclosed in the same envelope as the bid.\nBID BOND COMPANY:\n(BID BOND 10% OF BID)\nBIDDER:\n(FULL COMPANY NAME)\nPHONE/FAX/E-MAIL:\n\nN.Y.S. CERTIFIED MBE/WBE:\n(PLEASE PRINT WHICH ONE, IF NONE PLEASE PRINT N/A)\nEIN/SSN No.:\nBY:\n(PRINT NAME OF OWNER OR CORPORATE OFFICER)\n(SIGNATURE OF OWNER OR CORPORATE OFFICER)\nDATE:\nATTEST:\nNOTE:\n\n(EVERY SPACE MUST BE COMPLETED CORPORATE SEAL)\n(IF IT DOES NOT APPPLY, PLEASE INSERT N/A)\n\nIn case of any discrepancy between the price in words and that in figures the Lower Price Shall be considered the bid\nprice.\n*NAME OF THE PERSON OR FIRM THAT APPEARS ON THE LICENSE.\nALL BIDDERS: PLEASE USE THE FORM THAT IS PROVIEDED WITH THE PROJECT’S BID PACKAGE.\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\nBID FORM A-1\n\n\fEXHIBIT “A”\nARTICLE 15A\nMANDATORY NEW YORK STATE CERTIFIED\nMINORITY & WOMEN BUSINESS ENTERPRISES GOALS FOR SUBCONTRACTORS & SUPPLIES\n\nPROJECT NAME:\n\n11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump & Standpipe Replacement\n\nCONTRACT GOALS\nTOTAL % M/WBE GOAL\n30%\n\nContract # 1\n\nForm B‐1 “Bidder M/WBE Utilization Plan “in section “B” submitted by the lowest bidder will be compared to\nthe goals set forth above.\n\n14 A\n\n\fInsert bid breakdown pages\n\n\fOffice of Facilities Development/ Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442‐3680 Fax: (212) 442‐3741\n\nALTERNATES NO. 1 ‐ 6\n11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump &\nStandpipe Replacement\n\nNOTE:\n\nIMPORTANT\n\nThis solicitation contains Alternates 1‐6. The Corporation shall reserve the right select the Base Bid and /or\nAlternate No. 1 and / or Alternate No. 2. and/or Alternate No. 3., and/or Alternate No. , and/or Alternate No.\n5, and/or Alternate No. 6. In the event that the Corporation elects to award Alternate No. 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 or any\ncombination of Alternates No. 1-6, the responsive bidder submitting the lowest aggregate bid price (Base Bid\n+ Alternates Selected at the NYC HHC's Discretion) shall be determined to be the apparent lowest bidder for\nthis solicitation. The responsive bidder submitting the lowest base bid shall be determined to be the apparent\nlow bidder for this solicitation.\n\n\fOffice of Facilities Development/ Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442‐3680 Fax: (212) 442‐3741\n\nATTACHMET NO. 1 TO BID PROPOSAL\nALL CONTRACTS\nNOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO. 220 &\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO. 230\nAll contractors awarded contracts by New York City Health + Hospitals and all subcontractors working for those\ncontractors on New York City Health + Hospitals projects shall be required to notify each of their employees on\nsuch projects of the applicable prevailing wage for his or her job classification. This notification shall appear on\neach employee’s pay stub. In addition, the first paycheck given to employees at the project site, and the first\npaycheck given to employees at the project site after each successive July 1, shall be accompanied by a notice\nidentifying the public body. Such notice shall also inform employees of their right to contact the designated\npublic body if prevailing wages are not paid. Contact should be made through the Construction Management\nOffice of the New York City Health + Hospitals’ Facility where the work is being performed.\n\nAgreed:\nName of Contractor:\nBy: (Officer or Authorized) Representative: ________________________\nPrint\n__________________________________\nSignature\n\n__________________________\nDate\n\nTitle: ___________________________________________\nPrint\n\nBID FORM A‐1.1\n\n\fOffice of Facilities Development/ Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442‐3680 Fax: (212) 442‐3741\n\nName of Contractor: ___________________________\n\nProject Name: __________________________\n\nATTACHEMENT:\n\nNO. 2 TO BID PROPOSAL ‐ ALL CONTRACTS\n\nIMPROTANT:\n\nAll Insurance Carriers that will be providing coverage for New York Health + Hospitals\ncontacts shall be licensed and authorized/ admitted to be business in New York State.\n\nALL BIDDERS ARE REQUIRED TO COMPLETE THIS FORM AND SUBMIT IT WITH THEIR BID\n\nType of Coverage\n\nName of Insurance Carrier\n\nNAIC No.\n\nCommercial General Liability\nAutomobile Liability\nExcess/Umbrella\nWorker’s Compensation\nDisability Benefits\nAll Risk/Builders Risk\nIt is requested that an original Insurance Certificate substantiating the insurance coverage described above, be\nsubmitted to NYC H + H when the lowest responsive and responsible bidder returns its executed contract.\n\nSigned By: ________________________________________\n\nDate: ______________________________\n\nPrint Name: ________________________________________\nTitle: ______________________________________________\n\nBID FORM A‐1.2 Rev. 1/8/16\n\n\fFORM OF BID BOND\nKNOW ALL MEN BY THESE PRESENTS, that we__________________________________\n___________________________________________________________________________________\nhereinafter referred to as the “Principal,” and_______________________________________________\n__________________________________________________________________________________\nHereinafter referred to as the “Surety” are held and firmly bound to the New York City Health and Hospitals\nCorporation hereinafter referred to as the “Corporation” or to its successors and assigns, in the penal sum\nof_________________________________________________________________________________\n($______________________) Dollars, lawful money of the United States for the payment of which said sum of money will\nand truly to be made, we, and each of us, bind ourselves, our heirs, executors, administrators, successors, and assigns,\njointly and severally, firmly by these presents.\nWHEREAS, the Principal is about to submit (or has submitted) to the Corporation the accompanying proposal,\nhereby made a part hereof, to enter into a contract in writing\nfor________________________________________________________________________________________________\n__________________________________________________________________________________________________\nNOW, THEREFORE, the conditions of this obligation are such that the Principal shall not withdraw any Proposals\nwithout the consent of the Corporation for a period of forty‐five (45) days after the opening of bids, one hundred\nand twenty (120) days after the opening of bids where the project has one or more contracts with a bid of one\nmillion dollars ($1,000,000) or more and, in event of acceptance of the Principal’s Proposals by the Corporation if\nthe Principal shall:\nA.\n\nwithin five (5) days after notification by the Corporation execute and deliver six (6) copies to the\nCorporation of all the executed counterparts of the Contract in the form set forth in the Contract\nDocuments, in accordance with proposal as accepted;\n\nB.\n\nfurnish a Performance Bond and separate Payment Bond, as may be required by the Corporation for the\nfaithful performance and proper fulfillment of such Contract, which bonds shall be satisfactory in all\nrespects to the Corporation, shall be executed by good and sufficient sureties; and;\n\nC.\n\nin all respects performs the agreement created by the acceptance of said Proposal as provided in the\ninformation for Bidders, bound herewith and hereby made a part hereof, or if the Corporation shall reject\nthe aforesaid Proposal, then this obligation shall be null and void; otherwise to remain in full force and\neffect.\n\nIn the event that the Proposal of the Principal shall be accepted and the Contract be awarded to him, the Surety\nhereunder agrees, subject only to the payment by the Principal of the premium therefore, if requested by the\nCorporation to write the aforementioned Performance and Payment bonds in the form set forth in the Contract\nDocuments.\nIt is expressly understood and agreed that the liability of the Surety for any and all claims hereunder shall in no\nevent exceed the penal amount of this obligation as herein stated.\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\n\nBID FORM A‐2\n‐16‐\n\n\fThere shall be no liability under this bond if, in the event of acceptance of the Principals Proposal by the Corporation,\neither a Performance Bond or Payment Bond or both, shall not be required by the Corporation on or before the 30th day\nafter the date on which the Corporation signs the Contract.\nThe Surety, for value received, hereby stipulates and agrees that the obligations of the Surety and its bond shall\nin no way be impaired or affected by any postponements of the day upon which the Corporation will receive or\nopen bids, or by any extensions of the time within which the Corporation may accept the Principal’s Proposal or\nby any waiver by the Corporation of the requirements of the Information for Bidders; and the Surety hereby\nwaives notice of any such postponements, extensions or waivers.\n\nSURETY COMPANY MUST BE LICENSED TO DO BUSINESS IN THE STATE OF NEW YORK\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\n\nBID FORM A‐2\n\n‐17‐\n\n\fIN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Principal and the Surety have hereunto set their hands and seeks and such of them\nas are a Corporation have caused their corporate seals to be hereto affixed and these presents to be signed by\ntheir proper officers the ______________________ day of _______________in the year__________.\nBY _________________________________ (L.S.)\n(Principal Signature)\n\n(Seal)\n\nBY__________________________________\n(Surety Signature)\n\n(Seal)\n\nBY _________________________________\n*****************\nACKNOWLEDGMENT OF PRINCIPAL, IF A CORPORATION\n\nSTATE OF :___________________________)\nSS:\nCOUNTY OF _________________________)\nOn this _____________________ day of ______________in the year____________ before me\npersonally came_____________________________ to me known, who being by me duly sworn\ndid depose and say that he resides at_________________________________________________\n_______________________________________________________________________________\nthat he is the __________________________ of___________________________